{"timestamp":"2026-09-07T03:52:31.337Z","ordinal":16888,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_02be90ffdd5dff4a016a9e34fbe6ac87d097655893625beb3d","status":"completed","call_id":"call_drBVz9hSLNg5eZQW6Y25pI4y","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"tail -35 /Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-takeover/TAKEOVER.md\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise\",\"max_output_tokens\":1800}));\ntext(await tools.write_stdin({session_id:72866,chars:\"\",yield_time_ms:1000,max_output_tokens:1800}));\ntext(await tools.write_stdin({session_id:16064,chars:\"\",yield_time_ms:1000,max_output_tokens:1800}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749","create_time":1788753142.360631}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-07T03:52:31.427Z","ordinal":16889,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a07177-9855-71a2-89cd-4a9a37cdbfcb","turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-f06bab39-8802-4027-b068-49044667bc92","process_id":"55492","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","tail -35 /Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-takeover/TAKEOVER.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"tail -35 /Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-takeover/TAKEOVER.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"### IN PROGRESS: replace the architecture with one ordinary Git history\n\nThe user approved and requested implementation of the full \"Simplify dotfile tracking to one Git history\" plan. This supersedes the old architecture and review assumptions above. Exact file/directory mode=track enrollment only (no globs or track=true); no implicit global config, dotfiles.root, deployment outputs/sources, or symlink targets. Directory enrollment includes new descendants with capture exclusions. Tracking observation must coexist with deployment ownership. One ordinary Git branch/DAG retained indefinitely, automatic commits, manual sync delays pushing those same commits. No filtered shared history, share/private/local-only controls, backup policies/refs/uploads/encryption, or historical untracked-file undo. Keep shared-file encryption BEFORE any plaintext enters the repository, audit all reachable pushed commits, portable manifest/fresh bootstrap, native files, templates, variants, whole-setup conflict pause, default notifications. Only temporary interrupted-write journals/preimages outside publishable Git objects; discard after success/recovery, never expire unresolved transactions. No migration/compatibility machinery for unreleased formats, no personal-data deletion, no merge.\n\nNew isolated worktree: /Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise, branch codex/dotfiles-one-history, based on integrated top 2ea467a5e. All ten remote heads were verified unchanged before starting. Nothing from this rewrite has been pushed. Keep old PR worktrees intact until a coherent replacement is ready for redistribution/restacking.\n\nFirst slice currently edited (NOT whole implementation): tracked.rs only enrolls enabled mode=track requests, removes implicit roots and symlink target walking, skips inactive variants, excludes protected files from capture rather than retaining private history. Encrypted explicit credential files remain capturable, .local.toml excluded. Files composition keys tracking separately from deployment internally and permits tracking/deployment overlaps, while retaining deployment conflicts. Removed retention.rs and history.keep settings, removed automatic pruning, promotion compaction, and completed/no-op boundary deletion. Added tracking unit tests and e2e/cli/test_dotfiles_explicit_tracking. Legacy store/wrapper refs, promotion refs, share/backup fields, sync architecture, encryption boundary, onboarding, CLI, docs/blog still require replacement. Do NOT claim new model implemented or push this partial slice alone.\n\nVerified: initial cargo check --all-features PASS; 5 tracking unit tests PASS (1620). Current sessions: lint-fix 13300; system::files::tests 74575; explicit-tracking e2e build/run 28217. Use MISE_TRUSTED_CONFIG_PATHS=/Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN=1.95.0 mise ... for this new worktree. No subagents. Existing heartbeat updated to this rewrite and warned not to independently push/restack obsolete-design fixes. Continue the rewrite, not the prior review-only task.\n\n### One-history rewrite: subsequent integration progress (still unpushed)\n\nThe same integration worktree now writes ordinary parented commits on refs/heads/main. Commit trees contain tracked files directly, not snapshot/meta/blobs wrappers. Branch advancement is compare-and-swap; index reconstruction walks ordinary ancestry, uses commit OIDs for identity, and accepts normal Git commits. The actual commit tree overrides copied/stale message metadata. Manual-save and selective-save carry content from the ordinary parent; removed separate promotion refs and saved index. Retention remains removed. Current commit-message metadata still serializes a sanitized Checkpoint and MUST be replaced with minimal portable repository metadata; it is not the final format.\n\nCapture encrypts explicitly encrypted files before Git storage and reuses randomized ciphertext via a replaceable private fingerprint index. This is capture-only: legacy sync decryption/publication, manifest, recipient propagation, all-reachable plaintext auditing, and encrypted restore are NOT converted. Removed journal store_blob APIs and Blob.git; large preimages now stay in private sidecar files rather than Git. Temporary transaction lifecycle/cleanup and interrupted recovery still require conversion; do not claim that requirement finished.\n\nRemoved track --no-share/--no-backup/--private and associated emitted fields/examples. Other obsolete sharing/backup CLI/schema/config/internal fields remain pending wholesale removal. Untrack now filters observation declarations separately from deployment, permits referenced-source exclusions, commits enrollment removal, and leaves live files and historical commits intact. CLI tracking of a managed exact target still needs a declaration-storage solution without replacing deployment declarations. Protected-name checks now agree between walker and would_capture.\n\nVerified this slice: 6 shadow tests PASS (33612); 5 tracking tests PASS (92963); 4 journal tests PASS (3646); 35 deployment tests passed previously. Both new explicit_tracking and one_history e2es PASS (91473), and one_history including new untrack regression PASS (7788). lint-fix PASS (62761), diff --check PASS; cargo check reported source changed during compilation, so final shadow suite rerun is session 59686. Latest suite adds recovery-preimage object-store isolation and stale copied tree metadata assertions. No rewrite commits, pushes, PR edits, restacking, or blog changes yet.\n\nNext major work remains ordinary same-DAG synchronization (old filtered publication and backup modules still exist), portable enrollment/variant/encryption manifest with inactive variant preservation, temporary recovery lifecycle, complete shared encryption, fresh/local/remote bootstrap prerequisites, removal of remaining obsolete interfaces, docs/blog/render, focused and integrated verification, then distribute/restack with original expected remote heads. Do not publish the currently half-converted integration branch as merge-ready. Original PR worktrees and personal stores are untouched.\n\nLatest verification complete: all 7 shadow tests PASS (59686), including recovery preimages absent from Git objects and copied metadata not overriding the actual tree; cargo fmt --all -- --check PASS (47897). No running test sessions remain from this slice.\n\n### User requested push and continuation\n\nPushed the incomplete integration work to origin/codex/dotfiles-one-history, not the existing PR heads: d12dba51f (initial explicit single-history architecture) followed by c2eacab8a (remove backup transfers and audit ancestry). Existing PR heads remain untouched. git push also ran the repository-configured Entire hook.\n\nSecond commit switches the fetched branch to refs/remotes/origin/setup, removes recovery-ref fetching and sync's backup upload/replacement/pruning execution, deletes replacement/pruning functions, and replaces forced leased pushes with an observed-head check followed by normal Git push. Network unit tests pass, including unchanged intermediate ancestry and divergent rejection. Added all-ancestry encrypted-path audit, currently driven by active tracked encryption declarations, with tests that reject plaintext ancestors and second merge parents despite encrypted tip. Historical policy discovery still needs the repository manifest redesign. Tests pass (21441); lint-fix passes (77662) but reports remaining dead legacy backup code. Do not claim Clippy-clean or complete removal yet.\n\nContinued uncommitted edit moves the MessagePack Bytes type from backup encrypted.rs to shared files.rs, reversing the dependency so shared encryption no longer depends on the backup module. Cargo check running for this tiny extraction; inspect current processes/sessions before starting duplicate builds. Remaining architecture tasks above are unchanged. Continue implementation without waiting for another user prompt; user explicitly objected to stopping at intermediate test milestones.\n\nFurther cleanup in the same continuation removes `origin --purge`, its global `--yes` (only used by purge), the origin purge implementation, unused backup remote-ref enumeration, remote delete/atomic replacement methods, and obsolete atomic backup tests. No real remote refs/data were deleted. Latest lint-fix is session 42086; previous check passed with dead backup-code warnings. Those warnings still need removal with the remaining backup modules, not lint suppressions. Automation configuration verified ACTIVE at 30-minute cadence and already points to this integration rewrite.\n\nThat cleanup and Bytes extraction are now committed and pushed as bfefd402d on origin/codex/dotfiles-one-history. lint-fix 42086 completed successfully with the 12 known dead legacy backup warnings; push 90129 completed. No running commands remain. Integration branch upstream expected head is bfefd402d; original PR heads remain as listed earlier. Continue the implementation, not a review-only pass.\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"### IN PROGRESS: replace the architecture with one ordinary Git history\n\nThe user approved and requested implementation of the full \"Simplify dotfile tracking to one Git history\" plan. This supersedes the old architecture and review