{"timestamp":"2026-09-07T03:53:45.950Z","ordinal":16924,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a07177-9855-71a2-89cd-4a9a37cdbfcb","turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749","session_id":"01a07177-9855-71a2-89cd-4a9a37cdbfcb","root_turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749","response_id":"resp_02be90ffdd5dff4a016a9e354026cc87d09ef31a6d81f84f08","usage":{"input_tokens":128818,"cached_input_tokens":128128,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":241,"reasoning_output_tokens":129,"total_tokens":129059},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":13071276,"cached_input_tokens":12735360,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":43410,"reasoning_output_tokens":12132,"total_tokens":13114686},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":295093596,"cached_input_tokens":288207744,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":818424,"reasoning_output_tokens":192288,"total_tokens":295912020}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-07T03:53:50.956Z","ordinal":16925,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a07177-9855-71a2-89cd-4a9a37cdbfcb","turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-cf64a8b2-dc85-4d26-84cf-cd055a20e300","process_id":"63653","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,90p' src/system/history/sync/origin.rs; rg -n 'check|backup|share' docs/history.md | head -20"],"cwd":"file:///Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,90p' src/system/history/sync/origin.rs","name":"origin.rs","path":"src/system/history/sync/origin.rs"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'check|backup|share' docs/history.md","query":"check|backup|share","path":"history.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"//! Connecting, disconnecting, and purging the setup repository. Connecting\n//! discloses exactly what will happen before anything leaves the machine:\n//! the sync mode, what is shared per stream, what is not and why, what is\n//! backed up, secret-looking names, committed private content already in\n//! the repository's history, and how an existing unmarked repository would\n//! be adopted.\n\nuse std::collections::BTreeMap;\nuse std::path::PathBuf;\n\nuse eyre::{Result, bail};\nuse toml_edit::{Item, Value};\n\nuse super::SyncMode;\nuse super::format::{self, RepoState};\nuse super::layout::{Roots, is_configuration};\nuse super::network::{PUBLISH_REF, Remote, UPSTREAM_REF};\nuse super::run::{self, SyncRequest};\nuse super::{privacy, share};\nuse crate::file::display_path;\nuse crate::system::history::checkpoint::Store;\nuse crate::system::history::store::{self as hstore, Machine};\nuse crate::system::history::tracked::TrackedSet;\nuse crate::ui::prompt;\n\npub(crate) struct SetOptions {\n    pub url: String,\n    pub branch: String,\n    pub name: Option<String>,\n    pub mode: SyncMode,\n    pub yes: bool,\n}\n\n/// Connects the setup repository.\npub(crate) async fn set(store: &Store, tracked: &TrackedSet, opts: &SetOptions) -> Result<()> {\n    super::network::validate_url(&opts.url)?;\n    let mut preview_lock = Some(run::lock(store)?);\n    let repo = store\n        .repo()\n        .ok_or_else(|| eyre::eyre!(\"connecting requires git\"))?;\n    let previous_upstream = repo.ref_oid(UPSTREAM_REF)?;\n    let mut accepted = false;\n    let result = set_inner(store, tracked, opts, &mut accepted, &mut preview_lock).await;\n    if !accepted {\n        // Preview fetches must not change the active connection, even when\n        // validation or privacy checks fail before the prompt.\n        let mut cleanup_errors = Vec::new();\n        let restored = match previous_upstream {\n            Some(oid) => repo\n                .ref_oid(UPSTREAM_REF)\n                .and_then(|current| repo.update_ref(UPSTREAM_REF, &oid, current.as_deref())),\n            None => repo.delete_ref(UPSTREAM_REF),\n        };\n        if let Err(err) = restored {\n            cleanup_errors.push(format!(\"{UPSTREAM_REF}: {err:#}\"));\n        }\n        if !cleanup_errors.is_empty() {\n            let message = format!(\n                \"could not completely restore setup preview refs: {}; retry connecting before syncing\",\n                cleanup_errors.join(\"; \")\n            );\n            return Err(match result {\n                Err(err) => err.wrap_err(message),\n                Ok(()) => eyre::eyre!(message),\n            });\n        }\n    }\n    result\n}\n\nasync fn set_inner(\n    store: &Store,\n    tracked: &TrackedSet,\n    opts: &SetOptions,\n    accepted: &mut bool,\n    preview_lock: &mut Option<fslock::LockFile>,\n) -> Result<()> {\n    if opts.url.trim().is_empty() {\n        bail!(\"a repository url is required\");\n    }\n    let repo = store\n        .repo()\n        .ok_or_else(|| eyre::eyre!(\"connecting a setup repository requires git\"))?;\n    let state_dir = store.state_dir();\n    let mut machine = store.machine().clone();\n    if let Some(name) = &opts.name {\n        machine = Machine {\n            id: machine.id.clone(),\n            name: name.clone(),\n        };\n3:mise keeps checkpoints of your configuration files: the global mise config\n5:[track](/dotfiles.html#tracking-files-in-place) where it is. A checkpoint is\n13:A checkpoint holds files, not machine state. It does not journal other mise\n23:mise bootstrap dotfiles history diff                                       # what changed by hand since the latest checkpoint\n27:Without a connected origin, nothing leaves the machine: checkpoints live under\n29:sharing and remote backups according to the policies you review.\n31:## What a checkpoint records\n33:Every checkpoint carries:\n42:- **What changed** since the previous checkpoint, and a description computed\n47:  of an operation: `bootstrap-before` (the protective checkpoint taken before\n57:checkpoints the watcher saves. It gets one JSON object on stdin, `uuid`,\n69:The checkpoint is saved before the command runs and keeps its computed\n71:seconds. The command runs once per checkpoint the watcher saved, one at a\n75:`backup = false` never has its contents sent.\n77:## Referring to checkpoints\n80:`--path`, `latest~N` counts only the checkpoints where that path changed, so\n82:recent change however many other checkpoints came in between.\n91:mise bootstrap dotfiles history diff                        # working tree against the latest checkpoint\n92:mise bootstrap dotfiles history diff 12                     # what checkpoint 12 changed\n99:`mise bootstrap dotfiles save` records a checkpoint now. It fails when nothing could be\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"//! Connecting, disconnecting, and purging the setup repository. Connecting\n//! discloses exactly what will happen before anything leaves the machine:\n//! the sync mode, what is shared per stream, what is not and why, what is\n//! backed up, secret-looking names, committed private content already in\n//! the repository's history, and how an existing unmarked repository would\n//! be adopted.\n\nuse std::collections::BTreeMap;\nuse std::path::PathBuf;\n\nuse eyre::{Result, bail};\nuse toml_edit::{Item, Value};\n\nuse super::SyncMode;\nuse super::format::{self, RepoState};\nuse super::layout::{Roots, is_configuration};\nuse super::network::{PUBLISH_REF, Remote, UPSTREAM_REF};\nuse super::run::{self, SyncRequest};\nuse super::{privacy, share};\nuse crate::file::display_path;\nuse crate::system::history::checkpoint::Store;\nuse crate::system::history::store::{self as hstore, Machine};\nuse crate::system::history::tracked::TrackedSet;\nuse crate::ui::prompt;\n\npub(crate) struct SetOptions {\n    pub url: String,\n    pub branch: String,\n    pub name: Option<String>,\n    pub mode: SyncMode,\n    pub yes: bool,\n}\n\n/// Connects the setup repository.\npub(crate) async fn set(store: &Store, tracked: &TrackedSet, opts: &SetOptions) -> Result<()> {\n    super::network::validate_url(&opts.url)?;\n    let mut preview_lock = Some(run::lock(store)?);\n    let repo = store\n        .repo()\n        .ok_or_else(|| eyre::eyre!(\"connecting requires git\"))?;\n    let previous_upstream = repo.ref_oid(UPSTREAM_REF)?;\n    let mut accepted = false;\n    let result = set_inner(store, tracked, opts, &mut accepted, &mut preview_lock).await;\n    if !accepted {\n        // Preview fetches must not change the active connection, even when\n        // validation or privacy checks fail before the prompt.\n        let mut cleanup_errors = Vec::new();\n        let restored = match previous_upstream {\n            Some(oid) => repo\n                .ref_oid(UPSTREAM_REF)\n                .and_then(|current| repo.update_ref(UPSTREAM_REF, &oid, current.as_deref())),\n            None => repo.delete_ref(UPSTREAM_REF),\n        };\n        if let Err(err) = restored {\n            cleanup_errors.push(format!(\"{UPSTREAM_REF}: {err:#}\"));\n        }\n        if !cleanup_errors.is_empty() {\n            let message = format!(\n                \"could not completely restore setup preview refs: {}; retry connecting before syncing\",\n                cleanup_errors.join(\"; \")\n            );\n            return Err(match result {\n                Err(err) => err.wrap_err(message),\n                Ok(()) => eyre::eyre!(message),\n            });\n        }\n    }\n    result\n}\n\nasync fn set_inner(\n    store: &Store,\n    tracked: &TrackedSet,\n    opts: &SetOptions,\n    accepted: &mut bool,\n    preview_lock: &mut Option<fslock::LockFile>,\n) -> Result<()> {\n    if opts.url.trim().is_empty() {\n        bail!(\"a repository url is required\");\n    }\n    let repo = store\n        .repo()\n        .ok_or_else(|| eyre::eyre!(\"connecting a setup repository requires git\"))?;\n    let state_dir = store.state_dir();\n    let mut machine = store.machine().clone();\n    if let Some(name) = &opts.name {\n        machine = Machine {\n            id: machine.id.clone(),\n            name: name.clone(),\n        };\n3:mise keeps checkpoints of your configuration files: the global mise config\n5:[track](/dotfiles.html#tracking-files-in-place) where it is. A checkpoint is\n13:A checkpoint holds files, not machine state. It does not journal other mise\n23:mise bootstrap dotfiles history diff                                       # what changed by hand since the latest checkpoint\n27:Without a connected origin, nothing leaves the machine: checkpoints live under\n29:sharing and remote backups according to the policies you review.\n31:## What a checkpoint records\n33:Every checkpoint carries:\n42:- **What changed** since the previous checkpoint, and a description computed\n47:  of an operation: `bootstrap-before` (the protective checkpoint taken before\n57:checkpoints the watcher saves. It gets one JSON object on stdin, `uuid`,\n69:The checkpoint is saved before the command runs and keeps its computed\n71:seconds. The command runs once per checkpoint the watcher saved, one at a\n75:`backup = false` never has its contents sent.\n77:## Referring to checkpoints\n80:`--path`, `latest~N` counts only the checkpoints where that path changed, so\n82:recent change however many other checkpoints came in between.\n91:mise bootstrap dotfiles history diff                        # working tree against the latest checkpoint\n92:mise bootstrap dotfiles history diff 12                     # what checkpoint 12 changed\n99:`mise bootstrap dotfiles save` records a checkpoint now. It fails when nothing could be\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":3083},"formatted_output":"//! Connecting, disconnecting, and purging the setup repository. Connecting\n//! discloses exactly what will happen before anything leaves the machine:\n//! the sync mode, what is shared per stream, what is not and why, what is\n//! backed up, secret-looking names, committed private content already in\n//! the repository's history, and how an existing unmarked repository would\n//! be adopted.\n\nuse std::collections::BTreeMap;\nuse std::path::PathBuf;\n\nuse eyre::{Result, bail};\nuse toml_edit::{Item, Value};\n\nuse super::SyncMode;\nuse super::format::{self, RepoState};\nuse super::layout::{Roots, is_configuration};\nuse super::network::{PUBLISH_REF, Remote, UPSTREAM_REF};\nuse super::run::{self, SyncRequest};\nuse super::{privacy, share};\nuse crate::file::display_path;\nuse crate::system::history::checkpoint::Store;\nuse crate::system::history::store::{self as hstore, Machine};\nuse crate::system::history::tracked::TrackedSet;\nuse crate::ui::prompt;\n\npub(crate) struct SetOptions {\n    pub url: String,\n    pub branch: String,\n    pub name: Option<String>,\n    pub mode: SyncMode,\n    pub yes: bool,\n}\n\n/// Connects the setup repository.\npub(crate) async fn set(store: &Store, tracked: &TrackedSet, opts: &SetOptions) -> Result<()> {\n    super::network::validate_url(&opts.url)?;\n    let mut preview_lock = Some(run::lock(store)?);\n    let repo = store\n        .repo()\n        .ok_or_else(|| eyre::eyre!(\"connecting requires git\"))?;\n    let previous_upstream = repo.ref_oid(UPSTREAM_REF)?;\n    let mut accepted = false;\n    let result = set_inner(store, tracked, opts, &mut accepted, &mut preview_lock).await;\n    if !accepted {\n        // Preview fetches must not change the active connection, even when\n        // validation or privacy checks fail before the prompt.\n        let mut cleanup_errors = Vec::new();\n        let restored = match previous_upstream {\n            Some(oid) => repo\n                .ref_oid(UPSTREAM_REF)\n                .and_then(|current| repo.update_ref(UPSTREAM_REF, &oid, current.as_deref())),\n            None => repo.delete_ref(UPSTREAM_REF),\n        };\n        if let Err(err) = restored {\n            cleanup_errors.push(format!(\"{UPSTREAM_REF}: {err:#}\"));\n        }\n        if !cleanup_errors.is_empty() {\n            let message = format!(\n                \"could not completely restore setup preview refs: {}; retry connecting before syncing\",\n                cleanup_errors.join(\"; \")\n            );\n            return Err(match result {\n                Err(err) => err.wrap_err(message),\n                Ok(()) => eyre::eyre!(message),\n            });\n        }\n    }\n    result\n}\n\nasync fn set_inner(\n    store: &Store,\n    tracked: &TrackedSet,\n    opts: &SetOptions,\n    accepted: &mut bool,\n    preview_lock: &mut Option<fslock::LockFile>,\n) -> Result<()> {\n    if opts.url.trim().is_empty() {\n        bail!(\"a repository url is required\");\n    }\n    let repo = store\n        .repo()\n        .ok_or_else(|| eyre::eyre!(\"connecting a setup repository requires git\"))?;\n    let state_dir = store.state_dir();\n    let mut machine = store.machine().clone();\n    if let Some(name) = &opts.name {\n        machine = Machine {\n            id: machine.id.clone(),\n            name: name.clone(),\n        };\n3:mise keeps checkpoints of your configuration files: the global mise config\n5:[track](/dotfiles.html#tracking-files-in-place) where it is. A checkpoint is\n13:A checkpoint holds files, not machine state. It does not journal other mise\n23:mise bootstrap dotfiles history diff                                       # what changed by hand since the latest checkpoint\n27:Without a connected origin, nothing leaves the machine: checkpoints live under\n29:sharing and remote backups according to the policies you review.\n31:## What a checkpoint records\n33:Every checkpoint carries:\n42:- **What changed** since the previous checkpoint, and a description computed\n47:  of an operation: `bootstrap-before` (the protective checkpoint taken before\n57:checkpoints the watcher saves. It gets one JSON object on stdin, `uuid`,\n69:The checkpoint is saved before the command runs and keeps its computed\n71:seconds. The command runs once per checkpoint the watcher saved, one at a\n75:`backup = false` never has its contents sent.\n77:## Referring to checkpoints\n80:`--path`, `latest~N` counts only the checkpoints where that path changed, so\n82:recent change however many other checkpoints came in between.\n91:mise bootstrap dotfiles history diff                        # working tree against the latest checkpoint\n92:mise bootstrap dotfiles history diff 12                     # what checkpoint 12 changed\n99:`mise bootstrap dotfiles save` records a checkpoint now. It fails when nothing could be\n"},"started_at_ms":1788753230956,"completed_at_ms":1788753230956}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-07T03:53:51.012Z","ordinal":16926,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a07a00-3ca4-7c51-9e57-9d1f98177d4a","call_id":"call_R6PNHu8QAP974gwO8Eoqg27Y","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 5.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"1d2d54\",\"wall_time_seconds\":5.001930875,\"session_id\":16064,\"original_token_count\":0,\"output\":\"\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"d3b951\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000003083,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1180,\"output\":\"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 1180)\\nTotal output lines: 110\\n\\n//! Connecting, disconnecting, and purging the setup repository. Connecting\\n//! discloses exactly what will happen before anything leaves the machine:\\n//! the sync mode, what is shared per stream, what is not and why, what is\\n//! backed up, secret-looking names, committed private content already in\\n//! the repository's history, and how an existing unmarked repository would\\n//! be adopted.\\n\\nuse std::collections::BTreeMap;\\nuse std::path::PathBuf;\\n\\nuse eyre::{Result, bail};\\nuse toml_edit::{Item, Value};\\n\\nuse super::SyncMode;\\nuse super::format::{self, RepoState};\\nuse super::layout::{Roots, is_configuration};\\nuse super::network::{PUBLISH_REF, Remote, UPSTREAM_REF};\\nuse super::run::{self, SyncRequest};\\nuse super::{privacy, share};\\nuse crate::file::display_path;\\nuse crate::system::history::checkpoint::Store;\\nuse crate::system::history::store::{self as hstore, Machine};\\nuse crate::system::history::tracked::TrackedSet;\\nuse crate::ui::prompt;\\n\\npub(crate) struct SetOptions {\\n    pub url: String,\\n    pub branch: String,\\n    pub name: Option<String>,\\n    pub mode: SyncMode,\\n    pub yes: bool,\\n}\\n\\n/// Connects the setup repository.\\npub(crate) async fn set(store: &Store, tracked: &TrackedSet, opts: &SetOptions) -> Result<()> {\\n    super::network::validate_url(&opts.url)?;\\n    let mut preview_lock = Some(run::lock(store)?);\\n    let repo = store\\n        .repo()\\n        .ok_or_else(|| eyre::eyre!(\\\"connecting requires git\\\"))?;\\n    let previous_upstream = repo.ref_oid(UPSTREAM_REF)?;\\n    let mut accepted = false;\\n    let result = set_inner(store, tracked, opts, &mut accepted, &mut preview_lock).await;\\n    if !accepted {\\n        // Preview fetches must not change the active connection, even when\\n        // validation or privacy checks fail before the prompt.\\n        let mut cleanup_errors = Vec::new();\\n        let restored = match previous_upstream {\\n            Some(oid) => repo\\n                .ref_oid(UPSTREAM_REF)\\n                .and_then(|current| repo.update_ref(UPSTREAM_REF, &oid…180 tokens truncated…d: &mut bool,\\n    preview_lock: &mut Option<fslock::LockFile>,\\n) -> Result<()> {\\n    if opts.url.trim().is_empty() {\\n        bail!(\\\"a repository url is required\\\");\\n    }\\n    let repo = store\\n        .repo()\\n        .ok_or_else(|| eyre::eyre!(\\\"connecting a setup repository requires git\\\"))?;\\n    let state_dir = store.state_dir();\\n    let mut machine = store.machine().clone();\\n    if let Some(name) = &opts.name {\\n        machine = Machine {\\n            id: machine.id.clone(),\\n            name: name.clone(),\\n        };\\n3:mise keeps checkpoints of your configuration files: the global mise config\\n5:[track](/dotfiles.html#tracking-files-in-place) where it is. A checkpoint is\\n13:A checkpoint holds files, not machine state. It does not journal other mise\\n23:mise bootstrap dotfiles history diff                                       # what changed by hand since the latest checkpoint\\n27:Without a connected origin, nothing leaves the machine: checkpoints live under\\n29:sharing and remote backups according to the policies you review.\\n31:## What a checkpoint records\\n33:Every checkpoint carries:\\n42:- **What changed** since the previous checkpoint, and a description computed\\n47:  of an operation: `bootstrap-before` (the protective checkpoint taken before\\n57:checkpoints the watcher saves. It gets one JSON object on stdin, `uuid`,\\n69:The checkpoint is saved before the command runs and keeps its computed\\n71:seconds. The command runs once per checkpoint the watcher saved, one at a\\n75:`backup = false` never has its contents sent.\\n77:## Referring to checkpoints\\n80:`--path`, `latest~N` counts only the checkpoints where that path changed, so\\n82:recent change however many other checkpoints came in between.\\n91:mise bootstrap dotfiles history diff                        # working tree against the latest checkpoint\\n92:mise bootstrap dotfiles history diff 12                     # what checkpoint 12 changed\\n99:`mise bootstrap dotfiles save` records a checkpoint now. It fails when nothing could be\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749","create_time":1788753231.012805}}}
