t\":33,\"output\":\" docs/dotfiles.md | 72 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----------------------------\\n 1 file changed, 35 insertions(+), 37 deletions(-)\\n\"}","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_02be90ffdd5dff4a016a9e3a125e1c87d09933d07061d2c291","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"},{"call_id":"call_9XZfwJ4RTlfpcfslNVTttM2B","id":"ctc_02be90ffdd5dff4a016a9e3a131da087d08ded9a2bcfd0c0b6","input":"text(await tools.apply_patch(\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-takeover/TAKEOVER.md\\n@@\\n Portable-manifest/backup-interface slice pushed as 97fea0048 to origin/codex/dotfiles-one-history. Both e2es in16064 PASS; lint-fix49598 PASS; history.md revised to the new model (some paragraphs still need alignment as implementation completes). Original PR heads untouched. Current uncommitted continuation adds process-local transient Git-identity blobs: hash-object without -w, in-memory cat-object reads; decrypt no longer writes plaintext/payload objects or refs/mise-decrypted-files. Sync/live rollback comparisons and text merge results use transient blobs. Old publication code materializes only accepted unencrypted changes; encrypted ones still reencrypt there pending same-DAG rewrite. Encrypted-file tests44498 running. Replay comparison change landed just after build started, so rerun verification fresh as needed. Full same-DAG publication, manifest fresh onboarding, minimal metadata/notes replacement, lifecycle recovery, permissions and variant-aware restore still outstanding. Continue without waiting for user prompt.\\n+\\n+Transient plaintext slice: tests44498 found unchanged-ciphertext publication unnecessarily decrypting; fixed by skipping unchanged same-recipient ciphertext before unlocking. Fresh files tests88484 PASS6/6, shadow58577 PASS7/7. New e2e test_dotfiles_encrypted_capture first exposed a second direct capture bypass in cli/dotfiles/history/diff.rs (plaintext loose blob after read-only diff); fixed to use encrypted replay::live_tree. Fresh e2e91710 PASS: no plaintext object after capture, diff, rollback dry-run, or another save; no decrypted refs; config not implicitly enrolled. TransientObjects Debug prints counts only. lint-fix23187 passed before latest CLI/test edits; latest lint-fix93500 in progress. docs/bootstrap/setup.md and docs/dotfiles.md updated to explicit enrollment and no backups (hk may stage docs automatically).\\n+\\n+Next untracked file sync/graph.rs is preparatory ordinary-DAG code, NOT yet included in mod.rs, NOT compiled, and needs HistoryRepo::merge_base implementation. It provides Heads/Candidate, preserves existing fast-forward identities, merge parents, and expected local/remote refs with tests. Do not include it in the transient security commit until wired and verified; then integrate into run/publish/apply. Remaining old sync engine still builds filtered history and decrypts into transient comparison objects; encrypted restore currently still compares/writes ciphertext and needs conversion to decoded per-path operations. Variant-aware replay/diff and portable permission metadata remain. Fresh-machine enrollment and CLI exact managed-file tracking overlap need implementation; tracking --local still exists and must be removed. Scope temporary lifecycle and stale recovery, full-trailer/notes removal, and old dead-code cleanup still outstanding.\\n*** End Patch\"));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1788754449.217141,"turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_9XZfwJ4RTlfpcfslNVTttM2B","id":"ctco_01a07a13-21a7-7712-95f5-8008853aaee1","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1788754469.287465,"turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{}","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_02be90ffdd5dff4a016a9e3a29b5a487d0a9457333cc5ede74","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"},{"call_id":"call_P8fg1B4cnNkKZFw8ipqkWeNE","id":"ctc_02be90ffdd5dff4a016a9e3a2f0a2c87d0905e486c2e99b873","input":"text(await tools.apply_patch(\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise/src/system/history/sync/graph.rs\\n@@\\n     fn divergent_merge_keeps_both_parent_histories() {\\n@@\\n         assert_eq!(repo.output_tree_of(\u0026candidate.commit).unwrap(), merged);\\n     }\\n+\\n+    #[test]\\n+    fn unrelated_histories_are_never_adopted_over_local_commits() {\\n+        let temporary = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n+        let repo = HistoryRepo::open_or_init_in(temporary.path()).unwrap().unwrap();\\n+        let tree = tree(\u0026repo, b\\\"same contents are not shared ancestry\\\");\\n+        let local = repo.commit_tree(\u0026tree, vec![], \\\"local root\\\").unwrap();\\n+        let remote = repo.commit_tree(\u0026tree, vec![], \\\"remote root\\\").unwrap();\\n+        repo.update_ref(HistoryRepo::HISTORY_REF, \u0026local, None).unwrap();\\n+        repo.update_ref(UPSTREAM_REF, \u0026remote, None).unwrap();\\n+        assert!(Heads::read(\u0026repo).unwrap_err().to_string().contains(\\\"unrelated\\\"));\\n+        assert_eq!(repo.ref_oid(HistoryRepo::HISTORY_REF).unwrap(), Some(local));\\n+        assert_eq!(repo.ref_oid(UPSTREAM_REF).unwrap(), Some(remote));\\n+    }\\n }\\n*** End Patch\"));\ntext(await tools.write_stdin({session_id:93500,chars:\"\",yield_time_ms:1000,max_output_tokens:1200}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1788754470.102891,"turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"cu