{"timestamp":"2026-09-07T04:34:10.827Z","ordinal":17795,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a07a25-290b-7de2-ab7a-537ae4077fd9","call_id":"call_V5qfCEdMjUx2WKAR5WBWHlD4","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"7d7744\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000002333,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":972,\"output\":\"# CLAUDE.md\\n\\nThis file provides guidance to Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with code in this repository.\\n\\n## Build Commands\\n\\n- **Dev server**: `npm run start` (runs `hugo serve -w --buildDrafts`)\\n- **Production build**: `hugo --gc --minify --buildFuture`\\n- **Update TOCs**: `npm run toc` (regenerates table of contents in markdown files)\\n\\n## Architecture\\n\\nThis is a Hugo static site (blog) deployed to Netlify.\\n\\n- **Theme**: hugo-coder (in `themes/hugo-coder/`, git submodule)\\n- **Content**: Blog posts in `content/posts/` with date-prefixed filenames (e.g., `2024-04-13-shims-build-a-version-manager.md`)\\n- **Config**: `config.toml` for Hugo settings, `netlify.toml` for deployment\\n- **Static assets**: `static/` contains images, fonts, CSS customizations, and favicon files\\n- **Custom CSS**: `static/css/custom.css`\\n\\n## Hugo Version\\n\\nProduction uses Hugo 0.165.0 (see `netlify.toml`).\\n\\n## Post Frontmatter\\n\\nPosts use standard Hugo frontmatter with `title`, `date`, `draft`, etc. Many older posts redirect to external URLs (Medium, YouTube) via `netlify.toml` redirects.\\n\\n## Enterprise Page\\n\\nThe `/enterprise` page (`layouts/enterprise/single.html`) is a standalone landing page with its own design (not using the blog theme). The contact form submits to a Netlify function (`netlify/functions/enterprise-contact.js`) which sends email via Resend.\\n\\n### Stats that need periodic updating\\n\\nAll stats live in `layouts/enterprise/single.html`. To verify/update:\\n\\n- **MAU (300k)**: Check https://mise-versions.jdx.dev/stats\\n- **Homebrew ranking (#12)**: Check https://formulae.brew.sh/analytics/install-on-request/30d/\\n- **GitHub stars (25k+, mise)**: Check https://github.com/jdx/mise/stargazers\\n- **Supported tools (993)**: Check https://mise-versions.jdx.dev\\n- **Years of DX experience (\\\"12 years\\\")**: Count from July 2014 (Heroku start date)\\n- **hk downloads/month (25k)**: Update from hk download stats\\n- **2025 release count (211)**: Update annually from GitHub releases\\n- **2025 commit count (1,387)**: Referenced in copy, update annually\\n- **Terminal demo versions**: Update tool versions in the `mise use` terminal block with `mise latest <tool>`\\n\\nYou can also select platform-specific variants. For example, give macOS and Linux their own versions of `.zshrc`:\\n\\n```toml\\n[dotfiles]\\n\\\"~/.zshrc\\\" = { mode = \\\"track\\\", variants = [{ os = \\\"macos\\\" }, { os = \\\"linux\\\" }] }\\n```\\n\\nI still edit `~/.zshrc` on either machine. Changes on my Mac are saved and shared with other Macs; Linux changes stay with the Linux variant. Both versions live in the same repository, with their selectors in the same config file.\\n\\n## Templates still have a place\\n\\nTracking is my preferred starting point, but sometimes generating a file is exactly what you want:\\n\\n```toml\\n[dotfiles]\\n\\\"~/.zshrc\\\" = { mode = \\\"track\\\" }\\n\\\"~/.gitconfig\\\" = { source = \\\"templates/gitconfig.tera\\\", mode = \\\"template\\\" }\\n```\\n\\nThe template lives in your setup repository. When you run `mise bootstrap`, mise renders it into `~/.gitconfig` using that machine's settings.\\n\\nEdit the template when you want to change the generated configuration. For files you want to edit directly, like `.zshrc`, use tracking instead.\\n\\n## Secrets\\n\\nI'd keep secrets out of shared dotfiles. Use [mise's environment secrets](https://mise.jdx.dev/environments/secrets/) or [fnox](https://fnox.jdx.dev/) when an application can read them from the environment. If it needs a plaintext credential file, provision that separately and keep it out of shared history. Encrypted files can carry those contents through sync, but their live copies and local history remain plaintext. Configuration itself stays readable on the shared branch.\\n\\n## Try it\\n\\nYou don't need to migrate your whole setup to try it. Track a file, get the watcher running, make a few edits, and try rolling one back. Let me know what works for you and what still feels like too much setup.\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"6e78ec\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000001084,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1112,\"output\":\"~/.private-config  write  a file aa1f18c  a file 6c1889b\\nhistory: dry run; nothing was changed\\nSUCCESS: [mise bootstrap dotfiles rollback ~/.private-config --to 1 --dry-run] expected success\\nDEBUG: $ cat ~/.private-config\\nSUCCESS: [cat ~/.private-config] output is equal to 'second-private-value'\\nDEBUG: $ git --git-dir=/private/var/folders/6m/23f_80p95q79kmhpm8_w50340000gn/T/test_dotfiles_encrypted_capture.tBw01F/home/.local/state/mise/history/repo.git cat-file -e 6c1889b84a1f4a8cde1d9005c7b4219c397dc0d8\\nSUCCESS: [git --git-dir=/private/var/folders/6m/23f_80p95q79kmhpm8_w50340000gn/T/test_dotfiles_encrypted_capture.tBw01F/home/.local/state/mise/history/repo.git cat-file -e 6c1889b84a1f4a8cde1d9005c7b4219c397dc0d8] expected failure\\nDEBUG: $ git --git-dir=/private/var/folders/6m/23f_80p95q79kmhpm8_w50340000gn/T/test_dotfiles_encrypted_capture.tBw01F/home/.local/state/mise/history/repo.git cat-file -e aa1f18cc0aae150ae345e39c23f5de9fcf99f699\\nSUCCESS: [git --git-dir=/private/var/folders/6m/23f_80p95q79kmhpm8_w50340000gn/T/test_dotfiles_encrypted_capture.tBw01F/home/.local/state/mise/history/repo.git cat-file -e aa1f18cc0aae150ae345e39c23f5de9fcf99f699] expected failure\\nDEBUG: $ git --git-dir=/private/var/folders/6m/23f_80p95q79kmhpm8_w50340000gn/T/test_dotfiles_encrypted_capture.tBw01F/home/.local/state/mise/history/repo.git for-each-ref --format='%(refname)' refs/mise-decrypted-files refs/mise-history refs/machines\\nSUCCESS: [git --git-dir=/private/var/folders/6m/23f_80p95q79kmhpm8_w50340000gn/T/test_dotfiles_encrypted_capture.tBw01F/home/.local/state/mise/history/repo.git for-each-ref --format='%(refname)' refs/mise-decrypted-files refs/mise-history refs/machines]\\nDEBUG: $ mise bootstrap dotfiles save\\nmise history: saved checkpoint 2: edited ~/.private-config\\nSUCCESS: [mise bootstrap dotfiles save] expected success\\nDEBUG: $ git --git-dir=/private/var/folders/6m/23f_80p95q79kmhpm8_w50340000gn/T/test_dotfiles_encrypted_capture.tBw01F/home/.local/state/mise/history/repo.git cat-file -e aa1f18cc0aae150ae345e39c23f5de9fcf99f699\\nSUCCESS: [git --git-dir=/private/var/folders/6m/23f_80p95q79kmhpm8_w50340000gn/T/test_dotfiles_encrypted_capture.tBw01F/home/.local/state/mise/history/repo.git cat-file -e aa1f18cc0aae150ae345e39c23f5de9fcf99f699] expected failure\\nDEBUG: $ git --git-dir=/private/var/folders/6m/23f_80p95q79kmhpm8_w50340000gn/T/test_dotfiles_encrypted_capture.tBw01F/home/.local/state/mise/history/repo.git rev-list --count HEAD\\nSUCCESS: [git --git-dir=/private/var/folders/6m/23f_80p95q79kmhpm8_w50340000gn/T/test_dotfiles_encrypted_capture.tBw01F/home/.local/state/mise/history/repo.git rev-list --count HEAD] output is equal to '2'\\nDEBUG: $ mise bootstrap dotfiles rollback ~/.private-config --to 1 --yes\\n~/.private-config  write  a file aa1f18c  a file 6c1889b\\nmise history: rolled back ~/.private-config to checkpoint 1\\nSUCCESS: [mise bootstrap dotfiles rollback ~/.private-config --to 1 --yes] expected success\\nDEBUG: $ cat ~/.private-config\\nSUCCESS: [cat ~/.private-config] output is equal to 'first-private-value'\\nDEBUG: $ git --git-dir=/private/var/folders/6m/23f_80p95q79kmhpm8_w50340000gn/T/test_dotfiles_encrypted_capture.tBw01F/home/.local/state/mise/history/repo.git cat-file -e 6c1889b84a1f4a8cde1d9005c7b4219c397dc0d8\\nSUCCESS: [git --git-dir=/private/var/folders/6m/23f_80p95q79kmhpm8_w50340000gn/T/test_dotfiles_encrypted_capture.tBw01F/home/.local/state/mise/history/repo.git cat-file -e 6c1889b84a1f4a8cde1d9005c7b4219c397dc0d8] expected failure\\nDEBUG: $ git --git-dir=/private/var/folders/6m/23f_80p95q79kmhpm8_w50340000gn/T/test_dotfiles_encrypted_capture.tBw01F/home/.local/state/mise/history/repo.git cat-file -e aa1f18cc0aae150ae345e39c23f5de9fcf99f699\\nSUCCESS: [git --git-dir=/private/var/folders/6m/23f_80p95q79kmhpm8_w50340000gn/T/test_dotfiles_encrypted_capture.tBw01F/home/.local/state/mise/history/repo.git cat-file -e aa1f18cc0aae150ae345e39c23f5de9fcf99f699] expected failure\\nDEBUG: $ git --git-dir=/private/var/folders/6m/23f_80p95q79kmhpm8_w50340000gn/T/test_dotfiles_encrypted_capture.tBw01F/home/.local/state/mise/history/repo.git show HEAD:home/.private-config | head -1\\nSUCCESS: [git --git-dir=/private/var/folders/6m/23f_80p95q79kmhpm8_w50340000gn/T/test_dotfiles_encrypted_capture.tBw01F/home/.local/state/mise/history/repo.git show HEAD:home/.private-config | head -1] 'mise-encrypted-file-v1' is in output\\ncli/test_dotfiles_encrypted_capture: 10s\\n\\nFinished in 98.37s\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749","create_time":1788755650.827359}}}
