{"timestamp":"2026-09-07T04:36:23.305Z","ordinal":17858,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_02be90ffdd5dff4a016a9e3f42d92887d0b35d333a96d8a8a1","status":"completed","call_id":"call_z3TW3D2OiiRQMbxn9S6DWlPC","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"git push origin HEAD:refs/heads/codex/dotfiles-that-save-themselves\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/jdx/src/blog-dotfiles-history\",\"yield_time_ms\":1000,\"max_output_tokens\":700}));\ntext(await tools.write_stdin({session_id:66330,chars:\"\",\"yield_time_ms\":1000,\"max_output_tokens\":1000}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"tail -35 /Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-takeover/TAKEOVER.md\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise\",\"max_output_tokens\":1300}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749","create_time":1788755774.286597}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-07T04:36:23.324Z","ordinal":17859,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a07177-9855-71a2-89cd-4a9a37cdbfcb","turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749","session_id":"01a07177-9855-71a2-89cd-4a9a37cdbfcb","root_turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749","response_id":"resp_02be90ffdd5dff4a016a9e3f3e117087d089273960a534e37a","usage":{"input_tokens":128043,"cached_input_tokens":127488,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":249,"reasoning_output_tokens":24,"total_tokens":128292},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":30716731,"cached_input_tokens":30157696,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":103697,"reasoning_output_tokens":37611,"total_tokens":30820428},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":312739051,"cached_input_tokens":305630080,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":878711,"reasoning_output_tokens":217767,"total_tokens":313617762}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-07T04:36:24.544Z","ordinal":17860,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a07177-9855-71a2-89cd-4a9a37cdbfcb","turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-c8da5954-e5bb-4b82-a621-a14c3714671a","process_id":"40564","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","tail -35 /Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-takeover/TAKEOVER.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"tail -35 /Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-takeover/TAKEOVER.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"The same integration worktree now writes ordinary parented commits on refs/heads/main. Commit trees contain tracked files directly, not snapshot/meta/blobs wrappers. Branch advancement is compare-and-swap; index reconstruction walks ordinary ancestry, uses commit OIDs for identity, and accepts normal Git commits. The actual commit tree overrides copied/stale message metadata. Manual-save and selective-save carry content from the ordinary parent; removed separate promotion refs and saved index. Retention remains removed. Current commit-message metadata still serializes a sanitized Checkpoint and MUST be replaced with minimal portable repository metadata; it is not the final format.\n\nCapture encrypts explicitly encrypted files before Git storage and reuses randomized ciphertext via a replaceable private fingerprint index. This is capture-only: legacy sync decryption/publication, manifest, recipient propagation, all-reachable plaintext auditing, and encrypted restore are NOT converted. Removed journal store_blob APIs and Blob.git; large preimages now stay in private sidecar files rather than Git. Temporary transaction lifecycle/cleanup and interrupted recovery still require conversion; do not claim that requirement finished.\n\nRemoved track --no-share/--no-backup/--private and associated emitted fields/examples. Other obsolete sharing/backup CLI/schema/config/internal fields remain pending wholesale removal. Untrack now filters observation declarations separately from deployment, permits referenced-source exclusions, commits enrollment removal, and leaves live files and historical commits intact. CLI tracking of a managed exact target still needs a declaration-storage solution without replacing deployment declarations. Protected-name checks now agree between walker and would_capture.\n\nVerified this slice: 6 shadow tests PASS (33612); 5 tracking tests PASS (92963); 4 journal tests PASS (3646); 35 deployment tests passed previously. Both new explicit_tracking and one_history e2es PASS (91473), and one_history including new untrack regression PASS (7788). lint-fix PASS (62761), diff --check PASS; cargo check reported source changed during compilation, so final shadow suite rerun is session 59686. Latest suite adds recovery-preimage object-store isolation and stale copied tree metadata assertions. No rewrite commits, pushes, PR edits, restacking, or blog changes yet.\n\nNext major work remains ordinary same-DAG synchronization (old filtered publication and backup modules still exist), portable enrollment/variant/encryption manifest with inactive variant preservation, temporary recovery lifecycle, complete shared encryption, fresh/local/remote bootstrap prerequisites, removal of remaining obsolete interfaces, docs/blog/render, focused and integrated verification, then distribute/restack with original expected remote heads. Do not publish the currently half-converted integration branch as merge-ready. Original PR worktrees and personal stores are untouched.\n\nLatest verification complete: all 7 shadow tests PASS (59686), including recovery preimages absent from Git objects and copied metadata not overriding the actual tree; cargo fmt --all -- --check PASS (47897). No running test sessions remain from this slice.\n\n### User requested push and continuation\n\nPushed the incomplete integration work to origin/codex/dotfiles-one-history, not the existing PR heads: d12dba51f (initial explicit single-history architecture) followed by c2eacab8a (remove backup transfers and audit ancestry). Existing PR heads remain untouched. git push also ran the repository-configured Entire hook.\n\nSecond commit switches the fetched branch to refs/remotes/origin/setup, removes recovery-ref fetching and sync's backup upload/replacement/pruning execution, deletes replacement/pruning functions, and replaces forced leased pushes with an observed-head check followed by normal Git push. Network unit tests pass, including unchanged intermediate ancestry and divergent rejection. Added all-ancestry encrypted-path audit, currently driven by active tracked encryption declarations, with tests that reject plaintext ancestors and second merge parents despite encrypted tip. Historical policy discovery still needs the repository manifest redesign. Tests pass (21441); lint-fix passes (77662) but reports remaining dead legacy backup code. Do not claim Clippy-clean or complete removal yet.\n\nContinued uncommitted edit moves the MessagePack Bytes type from backup encrypted.rs to shared files.rs, reversing the dependency so shared encryption no longer depends on the backup module. Cargo check running for this tiny extraction; inspect current processes/sessions before starting duplicate builds. Remaining architecture tasks above are unchanged. Continue implementation without waiting for another user prompt; user explicitly objected to stopping at intermediate test milestones.\n\nFurther cleanup in the same continuation removes `origin --purge`, its global `--yes` (only used by purge), the origin purge implementation, unused backup remote-ref enumeration, remote delete/atomic replacement methods, and obsolete atomic backup tests. No real remote refs/data were deleted. Latest lint-fix is session 42086; previous check passed with dead backup-code warnings. Those warnings still need removal with the remaining backup modules, not lint suppressions. Automation configuration verified ACTIVE at 30-minute cadence and already points to this integration rewrite.\n\nThat cleanup and Bytes extraction are now committed and pushed as bfefd402d on origin/codex/dotfiles-one-history. lint-fix 42086 completed successfully with the 12 known dead legacy backup warnings; push 90129 completed. No running commands remain. Integration branch upstream expected head is bfefd402d; original PR heads remain as listed earlier. Continue the implementation, not a review-only pass.\n\n### Continued rewrite: portable manifest and removal of backup interfaces\n\nCurrent uncommitted work in dotfiles-one-history removes backup.rs/encrypted.rs/machines.rs and machine CLI, backup status/doctor/onboarding flags, per-file share/backup fields, and all machine recovery-ref constants/cleanup. Shared encryption remains in sync/files.rs. Deployment-source validation is separate required_sources bookkeeping, never enrollment. Portable layout is now home/... or config/... with @variant root suffixes, independent of deployment role. New manifest.rs records explicit enrollment, exclusions, public recipients, and all variants in the ordinary tree; capture carries inactive streams and repo-owned files from its ordinary parent, drops explicitly untracked streams. Manual/held capture paths use the selected variant. Manifest still needs portable full-permission metadata and fresh-machine import/provenance reconciliation; restore/diff callers still need variant-aware lookup. Sync state is now an atomic private JSON bookkeeping file, not refs/sync/state. Publication still uses the obsolete filtered builder and must be replaced; shared decryption still creates plaintext Git objects and must be fixed. Git notes and full sanitized checkpoint trailers also remain transitional.\n\nAncestry audit now unions encrypted-path policies from every reachable manifest including inactive variants and merge parents. Deleted origin backup fields from schema and regenerated schema; settings descriptions no longer advertise backups. No personal stores or remote refs were removed. Latest manifest unit tests 2/2 PASS (66348), previous shadow 7/7 PASS (58168), lint-fix PASS (22961) with remaining dead legacy warnings (not Clippy clean), render:schema PASS (72866). Current e2e session16064 builds/runs explicit_tracking and one_history; poll before edits/builds. Cargo check passed but one earlier compile overlapped source edits and mbx declined caching; subsequent lint check passed fresh. Continue implementation, then PR feedback/CI/conflicts; do not stop at these intermediate milestones or claim the original PRs updated.\n\nPortable-manifest/backup-interface slice pushed as 97fea0048 to origin/codex/dotfiles-one-history. Both e2es in16064 PASS; lint-fix49598 PASS; history.md revised to the new model (some paragraphs still need alignment as implementation completes). Original PR heads untouched. Current uncommitted continuation adds process-local transient Git-identity blobs: hash-object without -w, in-memory cat-object reads; decrypt no longer writes plaintext/payload objects or refs/mise-decrypted-files. Sync/live rollback comparisons and text merge results use transient blobs. Old publication code materializes only accepted unencrypted changes; encrypted ones still reencrypt there pending same-DAG rewrite. Encrypted-file tests44498 running. Replay comparison change landed just after build started, so rerun verification fresh as needed. Full same-DAG publication, manifest fresh onboarding, minimal metadata/notes replacement, lifecycle recovery, permissions and variant-aware restore still outstanding. Continue without waiting for user prompt.\n\nTransient plaintext slice: tests44498 found unchanged-ciphertext publication unnecessarily decrypting; fixed by skipping unchanged same-recipient ciphertext before unlocking. Fresh files tests88484 PASS6/6, shadow58577 PASS7/7. New e2e test_dotfiles_encrypted_capture first exposed a second direct capture bypass in cli/dotfiles/history/diff.rs (plaintext loose blob after read-only diff); fixed to use encrypted replay::live_tree. Fresh e2e91710 PASS: no plaintext object after capture, diff, rollback dry-run, or another save; no decrypted refs; config not implicitly enrolled. TransientObjects Debug prints counts only. lint-fix23187 passed before latest CLI/test edits; latest lint-fix93500 in progress. docs/bootstrap/setup.md and docs/dotfiles.md updated to explicit enrollment and no backups (hk may stage docs automatically).\n\nNext untracked file sync/graph.rs is preparatory ordinary-DAG code, NOT yet included in mod.rs, NOT compiled, and needs HistoryRepo::merge_base implementation. It provides Heads/Candidate, preserves existing fast-forward identities, merge parents, and expected local/remote refs with tests. Do not include it in the transient security commit until wired and verified; then integrate into run/publish/apply. Remaining old sync engine still builds filtered history and decrypts into transient comparison objects; encrypted restore currently still compares/writes ciphertext and needs conversion to decoded per-path operations. Variant-aware replay/diff and portable permission metadata remain. Fresh-machine enrollment and CLI exact managed-file tracking overlap need implementation; tracking --local still exists and must be removed. Scope temporary lifecycle and stale recovery, full-trailer/notes removal, and old dead-code cleanup still outstanding.\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"The same integration worktree now writes ordinary parented commits on refs/heads/main. Commit trees contain tracked files directly, not snapshot/meta/blobs wrappers. Branch advancement is compare-and-swap; index reconstruction walks ordinary ancestry, uses commit OIDs for identity, and accepts normal Git commits. The actual commit tree overrides copied/stale message metadata. Manual-save and selective-save carry content from the ordinary parent; removed separate promotion refs and saved index. Retention remains removed. Current commit-message metadata still serializes a sanitized Checkpoint and MUST be replaced with minimal portable repository metadata; it is not the final format.\n\nCapture encrypts explicitly encrypted files before Git storage and reuses randomized ciphertext via a replaceable private fingerprint index. This is capture-only: legacy sync decryption/publication, manifest, recipient propagation, all-reachable plaintext auditing, and encrypted restore are NOT converted. Removed journal store_blob APIs and Blob.git; large preimages now stay in private sidecar files rather than Git. Temporary transaction lifecycle/cleanup and interrupted recovery still require conversion; do not claim that requirement finished.\n\nRemoved track --no-share/--no-backup/--private and associated emitted fields/examples. Other obsolete sharing/backup CLI/schema/config/internal fields remain pending wholesale removal. Untrack now filters observation declarations separately from deployment, permits referenced-source exclusions, commits enrollment removal, and leaves live files and historical commits intact. CLI tracking of a managed exact target still needs a declaration-storage solution without replacing deployment declarations. Protected-name checks now agree between walker and would_capture.\n\nVerified this slice: 6 shadow tests PASS (33612); 5 tracking tests PASS (92963); 4 journal tests PASS (3646); 35 deployment tests passed previously. Both new explicit_tracking and one_history e2es PASS (91473), and one_history including new untrack regression PASS (7788). lint-fix PASS (62761), diff --check PASS; cargo check reported source changed during compilation, so final shadow suite rerun is session 59686. Latest suite adds recovery-preimage object-store isolation and stale copied tree metadata assertions. No rewrite commits, pushes, PR edits, restacking, or blog changes yet.\n\nNext major work remains ordinary same-DAG synchronization (old filtered publication and backup modules still exist), portable enrollment/variant/encryption manifest with inactive variant preservation, temporary recovery lifecycle, complete shared encryption, fresh/local/remote bootstrap prerequisites, removal of remaining obsolete interfaces, docs/blog/render, focused and integrated verification, then distribute/restack with original expected remote heads. Do not publish the currently half-converted integration branch as merge-ready. Original PR worktrees and personal stores are untouched.\n\nLatest verification complete: all 7 shadow tests PASS (59686), including recovery preimages absent from Git objects and copied metadata not overriding the actual tree; cargo fmt --all -- --check PASS (47897). No running test sessions remain from this slice.\n\n### User requested push and continuation\n\nPushed the incomplete integration work to origin/codex/dotfiles-one-history, not the existing PR heads: d12dba51f (initial explicit single-history architecture) followed by c2eacab8a (remove backup transfers and audit ancestry). Existing PR heads remain untouched. git push also ran the repository-configured Entire hook.\n\nSecond commit switches the fetched branch to refs/remotes/origin/setup, removes recovery-ref fetching and sync's backup upload/replacement/pruning execution, deletes replacement/pruning functions, and replaces forced leased pushes with an observed-head check followed by normal Git push. Network unit tests pass, including unchanged intermediate ancestry and divergent rejection. Added all-ancestry encrypted-path audit, currently driven by active tracked encryption declarations, with tests that reject plaintext ancestors and second merge parents despite encrypted tip. Historical policy discovery still needs the repository manifest redesign. Tests pass (21441); lint-fix passes (77662) but reports remaining dead legacy backup code. Do not claim Clippy-clean or complete removal yet