{"timestamp":"2026-09-07T04:52:57.369Z","ordinal":18186,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_02be90ffdd5dff4a016a9e430dedb087d0a293b0a781f2f4f5","status":"completed","call_id":"call_0ZC3FLABdkhMWGkgGJQw7RU2","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.apply_patch(\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-takeover/ONE_HISTORY_CURRENT.md\\n+# Current one-history continuation (2026-09-06)\\n+\\n+User explicitly says finish the plan, then feedback/checks/conflicts. Do not stop at a green intermediate slice. Do not merge. Original mise PR heads still untouched; implementation is in `/Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise`, branch `codex/dotfiles-one-history`.\\n+\\n+Latest integration push: `0bba94027` (push94883 verified). Previous `3adf709ec` includes manifest-only ordinary commit reading, graph primitives, decrypted restoration, removal of track --local, generated CLI docs. Blog PR99 pushed `72afed0` (push96894 verified); `/Users/jdx/src/blog-dotfiles-history` clean after one-history update. Hugo0.165.0 build passed. Blog still requires final factual review after implementation, including old example output counts.\\n+\\n+`0bba94027` removes filtered publication builder and refs/setup/publish. Runtime publish builds from ordinary HEAD with Graph::Heads/Candidate and audits candidate ancestry. Complete raw Git merge-tree must match already-applied local tree before adopting a merge; otherwise publication stops safely. Removed publication-time encryption delta/index code; encryption inventory now comes from manifest. Only format1 is supported. share comparison reads decoded transient objects with variant-aware tree paths. Capture dedup uses committed tree and modes, not machine-local coverage (coverage comparisons previously added a spurious empty commit on every sync).\\n+\\n+Verified: runtime publication unit tests2/2 PASS19798; encryption files tests5/5 PASS31999; manual ordinary-sync e2e initially failed39254 on spurious empty commits, fixed coverage comparison, PASS28538. Test verifies exact intermediate/local/remote commit identities, no extra commits on repeated sync, no separate refs, no implicit config capture, and encrypted commits identical before/after push with plaintext absent in both repositories. lint-fix11549 and render:usage45236 PASS. Dead-code warnings still remain; not Clippy clean.\\n+\\n+Current UNCOMMITTED continuation: `sync/run.rs` prepare derives baseline from common Git ancestry instead of persisted ack state; removes prepare's sync_state argument. `sync/reconcile.rs` early identical-saved/remote handling. New `e2e/cli/test_dotfiles_ordinary_two_machine` clones an ordinary bare store into a disposable second machine, connects, discards its operational sync-state cache, then fetches/pulls/publishes an incoming edit. Test session93910 running (build). Inspect result; do not assume success. No other running sessions known.\\n+\\n+Remaining architecture: complete same-DAG incoming adoption/merge including metadata and inactive streams; manifest-only fresh onboarding; effective enrollment reconciliation between Git and explicit configuration; CLI exact managed target overlap; minimal commit metadata replacing full Checkpoint and Git notes; portable permission metadata; variant-aware restore and plaintext diff without Git storage; temporary recovery lifecycle and retaining unresolved crash transactions; obsolete types/privacy paths/dead code; docs/blog/help audit; original PR distribution/restack with saved leases, CI and feedback. Existing graph merge currently blocks changes in repository-owned metadata because application only handles eligible live paths; encrypted divergent merges also need resolved ciphertext overlays after complete validation. Current baseline handles unique merge bases but criss-cross virtual-base reconciliation is still incomplete.\\n+\\n+Potential next internal design (not implemented): retain committed manifest enrollment as authority, apply deltas from explicitly changed local declarations using a private replaceable last-observed-declaration map. This avoids re-enrolling remotely untracked files from unchanged local config, and supports manifest-only machines without implicitly tracking global config. Must not create second file history or migration support. CLI exact managed-target tracking can use a dedicated global conf.d tracking declaration so deployment key is not overwritten; assess together with untrack and config precedence.\\n*** End Patch\"));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749","create_time":1788756745.476351}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-07T04:52:57.379Z","ordinal":18187,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a07177-9855-71a2-89cd-4a9a37cdbfcb","turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-a34fcdd7-7f92-49b4-b903-056bde7a454a","changes":{"/Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-takeover/ONE_HISTORY_CURRENT.md":{"type":"add","content":"# Current one-history continuation (2026-09-06)\n\nUser explicitly says finish the plan, then feedback/checks/conflicts. Do not stop at a green intermediate slice. Do not merge. Original mise PR heads still untouched; implementation is in `/Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise`, branch `codex/dotfiles-one-history`.\n\nLatest integration push: `0bba94027` (push94883 verified). Previous `3adf709ec` includes manifest-only ordinary commit reading, graph primitives, decrypted restoration, removal of track --local, generated CLI docs. Blog PR99 pushed `72afed0` (push96894 verified); `/Users/jdx/src/blog-dotfiles-history` clean after one-history update. Hugo0.165.0 build passed. Blog still requires final factual review after implementation, including old example output counts.\n\n`0bba94027` removes filtered publication builder and refs/setup/publish. Runtime publish builds from ordinary HEAD with Graph::Heads/Candidate and audits candidate ancestry. Complete raw Git merge-tree must match already-applied local tree before adopting a merge; otherwise publication stops safely. Removed publication-time encryption delta/index code; encryption inventory now comes from manifest. Only format1 is supported. share comparison reads decoded transient objects with variant-aware tree paths. Capture dedup uses committed tree and modes, not machine-local coverage (coverage comparisons previously added a spurious empty commit on every sync).\n\nVerified: runtime publication unit tests2/2 PASS19798; encryption files tests5/5 PASS31999; manual ordinary-sync e2e initially failed39254 on spurious empty commits, fixed coverage comparison, PASS28538. Test verifies exact intermediate/local/remote commit identities, no extra commits on repeated sync, no separate refs, no implicit config capture, and encrypted commits identical before/after push with plaintext absent in both repositories. lint-fix11549 and render:usage45236 PASS. Dead-code warnings still remain; not Clippy clean.\n\nCurrent UNCOMMITTED continuation: `sync/run.rs` prepare derives baseline from common Git ancestry instead of persisted ack state; removes prepare's sync_state argument. `sync/reconcile.rs` early identical-saved/remote handling. New `e2e/cli/test_dotfiles_ordinary_two_machine` clones an ordinary bare store into a disposable second machine, connects, discards its operational sync-state cache, then fetches/pulls/publishes an incoming edit. Test session93910 running (build). Inspect result; do not assume success. No other running sessions known.\n\nRemaining architecture: complete same-DAG incoming adoption/merge including metadata and inactive streams; manifest-only fresh onboarding; effective enrollment reconciliation between Git and explicit configuration; CLI exact managed target overlap; minimal commit metadata replacing full Checkpoint and Git notes; portable permission metadata; variant-aware restore and plaintext diff without Git storage; temporary recovery lifecycle and retaining unresolved crash transactions; obsolete types/privacy paths/dead code; docs/blog/help audit; original PR distribution/restack with saved leases, CI and feedback. Existing graph merge currently blocks changes in repository-owned metadata because application only handles eligible live paths; encrypted divergent merges also need resolved ciphertext overlays after complete validation. Current baseline handles unique merge bases but criss-cross virtual-base reconciliation is still incomplete.\n\nPotential next internal design (not implemented): retain committed manifest enrollment as authority, apply deltas from explicitly changed local declarations using a private replaceable last-observed-declaration map. This avoids re-enrolling remotely untracked files from unchanged local config, and supports manifest-only machines without implicitly tracking global config. Must not create second file history or migration support. CLI exact managed-target tracking can use a dedicated global conf.d tracking declaration so deployment key is not overwritten; assess together with untrack and config precedence.\n"}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA /Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-takeover/ONE_HISTORY_CURRENT.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1788756777379,"completed_at_ms":1788756777379}}
