{"timestamp":"2026-09-07T05:14:29.772Z","ordinal":18484,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a07177-9855-71a2-89cd-4a9a37cdbfcb","turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749","session_id":"01a07177-9855-71a2-89cd-4a9a37cdbfcb","root_turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749","response_id":"resp_02be90ffdd5dff4a016a9e4788a83487d087e676b1989a8661","usage":{"input_tokens":243392,"cached_input_tokens":242048,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":5507,"reasoning_output_tokens":0,"total_tokens":248899},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":44842935,"cached_input_tokens":44103168,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":157449,"reasoning_output_tokens":63792,"total_tokens":45000384},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":326865255,"cached_input_tokens":319575552,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":932463,"reasoning_output_tokens":243948,"total_tokens":327797718}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-07T05:14:29.782Z","type":"compacted","payload":{"compaction_response_id":"resp_02be90ffdd5dff4a016a9e4788a83487d087e676b1989a8661","first_window_id":"01a07177-9855-71a2-89cd-4aa0d35d1afe","guardian_history":[{"content":[{"text":"that is not a public repo\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071f1-fe09-7c21-af08-a3fa8298bd79","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788618079.753048,"turn_id":"01a071f1-fbf7-72f3-9457-0a3df2c9aea2"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"the rcm involved a lot of custom flaky code and complex cli commands, it was a pain to onboard new boxes too. mise not only simplifies that but it has much more capability\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071f3-9fac-7e90-adb8-a1d6d0c90799","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788618186.668571,"turn_id":"01a071f3-9e5a-7b40-829a-5323e4ea8a06"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"i think we should hit on integrating with mise bootstrap so setup is just `mise bootstrap --from-git`\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071f4-3df7-7401-9336-f2dc79df2e7e","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788618227.191596,"turn_id":"01a071f4-3d2d-72b3-a014-63717c451580"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"saying that though, it's not enough since my dotfiles repo will be private. so there will be some initial setup like installing mise and setting up git auth before i can use it, could we improve that workflow with mise?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071f5-0f90-74d0-9392-e18a23ceeb1b","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788618280.848926,"turn_id":"01a071f5-0db4-7ea2-994a-15e681b94e59"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"maybe read through my past blog posts to make this sound like i am writing it too\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071f6-19b8-7f42-ab51-851bfd4da8f0","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788618348.98467,"turn_id":"01a071f6-18da-7f53-bc17-3250d9acf58a"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"i like your suggestion about --from-git improvements, let's include that in the plan, but before that, but before that maybe we could think about the current GITHUB\\_TOKEN setup stuff? we have a lot of ways to configure that\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071fa-b84e-7693-a40f-59aa242f4866","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788618651.726768,"turn_id":"01a071fa-b793-75c2-bc53-4642c3e2b72c"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"personally i would probably want to go with the oauth thing\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071fc-a14e-7be2-a960-32a74231b812","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788618776.910471,"turn_id":"01a071fc-a0a0-7a12-a1de-868a787d0155"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"i think this could go into the blog post, and maybe as a callout tip for the docs but generally the oauth app would be optinoal, i think users would need to setup gh and auth themselves—which they can install with mise\n\nso i think `curl mise.run, mise x gh -- gh auth login`, mise bootstrap --form-git\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071fd-eacd-77b2-a1eb-996733f54563","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788618861.261747,"turn_id":"01a071fd-ea15-7f61-9f79-0ac7634d9740"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"or alternatively we should have a workflow for mise bootstrap remote, ideally where we can somehow share the token with the remote box. i think what would be really cool in fact is if we didn't need to put the token on the box and instead could use the host as a proxy to talk to github\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a071ff-131b-7030-a3f5-4aed4285648b","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788618937.115176,"turn_id":"01a071ff-1268-79a3-b250-d5a95b9d1692"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\n# Files pasted by the user:\n\n## \"# Plan: bootstrap adopts and recreates the setup; `[dotfiles]` declares file ma…\": /Users/jdx/.codex/attachments/e48b166e-161b-49a3-9d17-7c4072d06ac9/pasted-text.txt\n\n## My request:\nneat idea, i have another agent working on it now.\n\nNow, take what we've discussed and review the latest plan draft\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07200-d4aa-7252-aab7-90aeccdc0f63","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788619052.202824,"turn_id":"01a07200-d3e2-7901-8d8b-e0fffa61dcaa"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"question, when they use --from-git does it get stored as a bare repo?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07207-6c07-7342-9df1-c086bb20cdf9","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788619484.167703,"turn_id":"01a07207-6b43-72c0-a2b7-71529f2f0bb9"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"yeah let's simplify it, but we need backwards compat\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07207-c328-7b83-9438-5736c71705a7","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788619506.47214,"turn_id":"01a07207-c277-7cf0-868b-80483eded2c5"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"ok but if they use a bare repo, how are they able to use something like templates?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07208-c193-7081-aa2c-0c30e99f4555","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788619571.603653,"turn_id":"01a07208-c0e2-7981-a1e4-ab12890522e9"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"so they'd also probably need to track the templates?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07209-8758-7ef0-8ce5-8e0bb8b4222a","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788619622.23257,"turn_id":"01a07209-86a7-7c53-a49e-001dab1bbb3c"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"agreed. so it sounds like if they want tracking they need to use bare\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0720a-4590-7d82-9574-2f1099450607","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788619670.928459,"turn_id":"01a0720a-44d0-7003-8d68-d8852a3fac33"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"show me some exapmles\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0720a-c7a8-7d42-b948-61e9c91a705c","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788619704.232919,"turn_id":"01a0720a-c6f7-77d2-87a3-e0724fdc0290"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"oh so it's fine because we never actually managed the git repo before\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0720b-ec41-7333-a87a-409cfd0f93c7","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788619779.137851,"turn_id":"01a0720b-eb8c-7750-b552-2024a1f14171"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"ok give me the full instructions to send to the other agent including your last corrections\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0720c-2f47-7d83-825e-8341cf0b303b","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788619796.295168,"turn_id":"01a0720c-2e95-7741-8779-12b0e88a3d29"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\n# Files pasted by the user:\n\n## \"# Plan: bootstrap adopts and recreates the setup; `[dotfiles]` declares file ma…\": /Users/jdx/.codex/attachments/e4d99c20-8c58-438f-8ec9-d7f84685c0a4/pasted-text.txt\n\n## My request:\nreview \n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0721e-1748-71d1-88e8-d50fb16b2706","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788620969.800992,"turn_id":"01a0721e-1689-77a2-900c-63c2c3b82ba8"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"make a pr for that blog post\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a072e7-edfa-7c20-a213-ad4942c9ef99","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788634197.498089,"turn_id":"01a072e7-ec26-7300-9c9a-a4025ab5295a"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"rebase the blog pr\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a072e8-0e8f-7411-ac1d-f697e67f25ac","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788634205.839443,"turn_id":"01a072e7-ec26-7300-9c9a-a4025ab5295a"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"i believe all the prs are up, how does it look? how does it compare to the blog post?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07307-f793-7242-ae30-ac6e498dc712","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788636297.107288,"turn_id":"01a07307-f67e-7aa2-a103-fc48da7a7417"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"i'm wondering if it should be `mise history` or `mise bootstrap history`\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07348-9d82-72d0-8f35-1cb7fc6eeba4","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788640533.890321,"turn_id":"01a07348-9c97-7dc1-be2a-a4ddbb3f55b4"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"on the blog post\n\nI think we're explaining too much about rcm details\n\n\"and the part I'm most excited about is the integration with `mise bootstrap`\" it is part of mise bootstrap so that sounds weird\n\nsee the pr i landed with `mise ssh`, we should incorporate that into the blog post and later the pr stack\n\"private, btw,\" - remove the \"btw\"\n\n\"mise installs and runs `gh`, so you don't need to install it separately\" - obviously, but we should use the proxy thing from the mise ssh thing anyhow\n\nwe should show output for commands like \"mise bootstrap\"\n\n\"If the watcher isn't running, mise warns you and tells you how to set it up. Adding a file saves its current contents, but obviously it can't keep saving changes without something watching it.\" i think we can strike this\u0026#x20;\n\n\"After a short pause,\" how does the debouncing work exactly? I think it should be fairly complex, like save reasonably quick after a change unless the same file keeps beign modified or something, like have some sort of backoff? it's probably also worth explaining what happens if the user adds a noisy file (which we should tell them not to)\n\n\"Files ending in `.local.toml`, including mise's `config.local.toml`, are protected from sharing by default—even when you enroll their parent directory. They can still have local recovery history, and their remote backups follow the backup and encryption policies. If you deliberately want to share one, you can explicitly override that protection for the file.\" remove that\n\n\"Connecting an existing repository also checks outgoing history for private files that were already committed. Adding an ignore rule today doesn't make yesterday's commit private.\" - remove\n\n\nremove the section on chezmoi\n\nmake the section about secrets a lot shorter\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0736d-6ba9-7e13-82fc-05caacbd1e75","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788642945.961264,"turn_id":"01a0736d-6a8a-7773-ac4f-584d4500af7b"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"that seems way too short, also, how does warning actually work when it's running as a service?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07370-910b-7893-937d-d50a3e131571","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788643152.139706,"turn_id":"01a07370-903b-76b1-a7da-36cec20f393b"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"i think it should go up to like 24 hours if the file continuously changes\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07371-0ac0-7552-95e3-3bf1285f28b5","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788643183.296302,"turn_id":"01a07371-09f5-7f72-86c0-729423541b84"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"ok edit the blog post to mention this, it doesn't need a lot of detail, i'll later have you instruct the other agent about this decision\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07371-7c12-7bd3-b45e-b6def9c1541e","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788643212.306618,"turn_id":"01a07371-7b50-7cb0-8378-37b5ea3403a7"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"the first time we mention mise bootstrap we should link to it\n\nI don't think we should use `mise ssh`, we should use `mise bootstrap remote` with the right flags for the github proxy\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07372-cf65-73e2-a6c3-0b98f9bd637a","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788643299.173311,"turn_id":"01a07372-ce80-7131-b302-8e2a3827cff0"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"make this non-draft\n\nuse 'jdx/dotfiles' as my repo name\n\nwhat happens when there is a conflict when the service is running?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07376-2f97-7b22-ac73-2ed539030471","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788643520.40775,"turn_id":"01a07376-2ed7-7143-a8f1-03f0b1614350"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"The GitHub token stays on my laptop, and borrowed access ends when the bootstrap run finishes. This currently works between Linux and macOS machines. It’s read-only setup access, not permanent sync authentication: a remote machine that should push its own changes later still needs write credentials.\n\nmention after this `mise ssh` can be used for permanent sessions\n\n\"plus mise-managed recovery history for individual machines\" - is this sent to the origin repo?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07379-41fe-7fe0-b71c-839b946bd250","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788643721.726146,"turn_id":"01a07379-412a-7d53-87cc-3ca28df3adc5"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\"You don’t need a second repository just for templates.\" - this doesn't need to be said\n\nthe `mise ssh` thing can go into a tip callout\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0737b-7694-7e71-a607-62291e84c951","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788643866.260493,"turn_id":"01a0737b-75b6-7e22-abea-31c6e80a0c3c"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"i'm wondering if we conflated dotfile history with history of bootstrap apply things like installing packages\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0737c-6f99-7db2-9c78-59b7ccfc5c67","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788643930.009396,"turn_id":"01a0737c-6eda-7ef0-b918-3fd62ff6eedf"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"not really sure `mise history` makes sense, users would expect it to apply to things like `mise install` and `mise set`\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0737d-2404-7f53-b5b2-ce691eff326e","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788643976.196335,"turn_id":"01a0737d-2348-78f1-af8c-de230abba0f0"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"i also wonder if we should remove the journaling and stuff for non-file cahnges\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0737d-99ac-7600-8238-70e1b92f03a9","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788644006.316862,"turn_id":"01a0737d-98f2-77b2-aec3-5df661c0d2c9"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"in that case I think it should all live inside `mise bootstrap` commands too\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0737e-4869-73f1-b3a7-805b2e8ce6c2","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788644051.049767,"turn_id":"01a0737e-479d-7d91-8c4b-9744b093f8bf"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"give me some instructions for the agent about this and the mise ssh stuff since it's in progress\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0737e-ac5a-7381-b563-806d9946f3ef","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788644076.634472,"turn_id":"01a0737e-ab89-7703-852e-bb746aaf852e"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"also edit the blog post to reflect this\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0737f-764f-7fc0-8872-ae402cbf7c78","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788644128.335156,"turn_id":"01a0737f-758c-7303-b0c9-9ac7f8e975b7"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"## 5. Make background problems visible\n\nhow on earth are we going to achieve this?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07380-2d4d-7952-a113-2e16850f7f57","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788644175.181632,"turn_id":"01a07380-2c90-76d0-be86-b438c1261a9e"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"we could use mise doctor\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07380-8245-7781-8c49-ed7ecae219c1","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788644196.933533,"turn_id":"01a07380-817a-7b90-af6a-34fcce586871"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"ok give me the full instructions again\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07380-b864-7951-bca3-aa19cd1ec001","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788644210.788339,"turn_id":"01a07380-b791-71a2-83ed-8ee57a284a28"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Omarchy was a big motivation for this. I want users to keep editing their native config files, including having agents edit them, and have mise take care of the history and setup. You shouldn’t need to translate your configuration into another language to get that. This doesn’t automatically merge your customizations with distro updates though, or replace an OS snapshot.\n\n- remove that paragraph\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07387-6158-7343-ab81-76f1b5b86b8a","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788644647.256247,"turn_id":"01a07387-5f77-7743-b919-562cca7273b1"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"You can also select platform-specific variants. - we should show an example of this\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07387-f4ef-7500-8697-8f60102eeec5","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788644685.039369,"turn_id":"01a07387-f429-78d1-8664-59cf1e17d782"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"These work together. The template source travels with the shared setup, and bootstrap renders it using the destination machine’s inputs. The generated `.gitconfig` isn’t shared as though it were the source.\n\nIf you edit the generated file, local history can help recover that edit, but the next render may replace it. mise doesn’t pretend it can reverse a rendered file back into a template.\n\nExisting symlink, copy, and managed-edit workflows still work. You don’t have to migrate a setup you’re happy with. There are also recipes for mixed-platform setups, templates, and moving an existing dotfiles repository to tracking.\n\n- that section is confusing to me\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07388-6f93-70b3-85b7-5eec9664a7ee","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788644716.435732,"turn_id":"01a07388-6ed0-7e42-8a09-237a1f8c1fd6"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"ok do that, then give the entire post a read through and make improvmeent suggestions\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07388-e96d-7573-aed4-dfe1fa1b6f98","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788644747.629587,"turn_id":"01a07388-e8b4-7ce2-8345-dbf484d062a1"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"do all of that\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07389-f0b6-7ad1-a9e5-72d9e5025dd5","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788644815.030702,"turn_id":"01a07389-efeb-74d0-b6b0-dcef9389f100"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"background history service ? remove that\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0738c-6062-71c2-939e-be54dcc65df8","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788644974.690759,"turn_id":"01a0738c-5faa-7b73-ab44-6d93a9f5ab50"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"This is file history, not a record of everything mise does. Bootstrap saves configuration before and after changing it, but restoring those files doesn’t reverse package installations or service state changes. Rolling back an `ffmpeg` declaration, for example, leaves the installed package alone.\n\n- no user would assume this\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0738d-e3a9-7b73-9778-e3dbf42b2a1f","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788645073.833476,"turn_id":"01a0738d-e2da-7bb2-ab0b-e929cc75866d"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"maybe show the example config for configuring it with claude\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0738e-5d9c-7453-8e9c-39e3dc2d5e1e","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788645105.05287,"turn_id":"01a0738e-5ce3-7082-8ce1-468c17181e11"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"i think we should have a setting for optional desktop notifications on sync conflicts\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0738f-26c2-7b01-9970-17e8fe3cfe2c","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788645156.546013,"turn_id":"01a0738f-25fc-79b1-b737-08d74520d422"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"add that to the blog, just a brief mention\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0738f-7aba-74e3-8645-37fe7d2735f9","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788645178.04221,"turn_id":"01a0738f-7a01-73a0-8185-1297a2de28b6"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"review the pr stack\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07400-afd5-7ec2-828e-f320ccbcf4bd","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788652597.205801,"turn_id":"01a07400-aea6-70a1-b6b4-e8a3bf84b419"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"post comments\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07402-1594-75d0-a304-f67339be4807","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788652688.788864,"turn_id":"01a07402-14ca-7311-a89c-d39b9c2488bd"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"post the comments, including the gaps and alignment issues, why can't you use gh?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07402-d91a-7483-8e2d-cf9a836faa15","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788652738.842006,"turn_id":"01a07402-d852-7043-8d30-4870c1fd9dca"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"were those the only ones that needed comments?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07405-8594-7531-bbbd-9a18551bc088","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788652914.06827,"turn_id":"01a07405-84c6-7ac3-ab1a-d4bd9c5a8162"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"ok look at all of the prs\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07405-f418-7320-a0b8-cc9a2d132521","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788652942.360742,"turn_id":"01a07405-f35d-7971-a9c9-4b757f525c8d"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"post comments\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0740a-f88b-7df1-b91b-56a2f910c3e5","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788653271.179205,"turn_id":"01a0740a-f7bb-7c01-a437-621f4990b698"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"how is the stack looking now?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a074e9-f23c-7e41-9a86-ab42df6d83c3","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788667884.092092,"turn_id":"01a074e9-f029-7b41-9d5b-15393cc141f0"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"post comments\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a074ec-fc37-74c0-b8df-4d09b70172d5","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788668083.255237,"turn_id":"01a074ec-fb3a-7160-80ce-1cf4ecb0fe8d"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"give it another pass, post comments\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07545-ab74-7600-aeb9-346c3511708b","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788673895.284972,"turn_id":"01a07545-a993-7112-87cf-c926ae1d5134"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"are there gaps?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07548-8155-7210-8ff5-0d860b19e3a8","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788674081.109154,"turn_id":"01a07548-8077-7b63-a03f-e67f62bdd635"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"ok give me instructions for the agent to close the gaps\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07549-99af-79b3-b211-7642ae906637","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788674152.879463,"turn_id":"01a07549-98e7-7e42-b49a-91290a55dcd5"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"how does the stack look now?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07744-b60c-7252-a02c-c727bdb84656","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788707386.892536,"turn_id":"01a07744-b3c8-76e0-81d3-d3d855644ad2"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"the goal was to have it sync individual files even if some were conflicted, right?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07748-5782-7853-a8cd-174e7f0a7cff","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788707624.834069,"turn_id":"01a07748-56c2-7e20-b4ff-4dff4121c93a"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"i'm wondering if we should keep that or have everything move atomically\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07748-c321-7241-80a2-db0910994ff8","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788707652.385885,"turn_id":"01a07748-c24c-72c1-ad65-85ec7f832d0e"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"i kind of think \"sync stopped working\" is good since without the notifications users won't know they have conflicts and they're not going to bother with atomic groups\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07749-753f-7742-a6f0-c1bcd9838436","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788707697.983667,"turn_id":"01a07749-747e-7080-a0e4-96ca8555a97b"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"i think we should turn on notifications by default. if we get rid of partial sync does that make things simpler or harder?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0774a-485a-7c71-8195-7d2fdd590023","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788707752.026807,"turn_id":"01a0774a-478b-7463-8a04-94897d52f450"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"ok\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0774a-fe9c-7d01-8068-b5033e0ee88d","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788707798.684623,"turn_id":"01a0774a-fdcb-7792-8eb7-c035721bc8dc"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"ok i want you to take over working on these PRs now. \n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0774b-677c-7bf2-9038-a448cc9a6cfd","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788707825.532997,"turn_id":"01a0774b-66c1-7263-b21d-973c6f6715af"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"PLEASE IMPLEMENT THIS PLAN:\n# Take over the dotfiles PR stack\n\n## Summary\n\nTake exclusive ownership of the six existing PRs, finish implementation and review fixes, and deliver a verified, merge-ready stack. The other agent stops pushing. Do not merge the PRs.\n\nPreserve the established design: native-file editing, mise-owned history, bootstrap onboarding, platform variants, and template compatibility.\n\n## Implementation\n\n### Whole-setup conflict handling\n\nReplace partial synchronization with this contract:\n\n- Any unresolved conflict pauses shared-branch publication and incoming application for the entire setup.\n- Local checkpoints, fetching, and eligible machine-recovery backups continue.\n- Compute conflicts across the complete eligible setup before publishing or writing incoming files.\n- Keep per-file resolution choices, but record those choices without partially applying the setup. Resume only after all conflicts are resolved.\n- Recompute and validate the plan against current local and remote versions before resuming. A later edit invalidates any resolution based on an older version.\n- Preserve explicit path selection for local rollback; it must not become a way to bypass the global sharing pause.\n\nPreflight the complete incoming batch, including newly declared files and required template sources. Keep protective checkpoints and journaling for mid-write failures. Attempt safe recovery without overwriting concurrent user edits; persist an actionable failure if recovery cannot complete. Describe this as all-or-nothing application, not truly atomic filesystem writes.\n\n### Notifications and health\n\n- Default `history.notify` to true; preserve explicit false settings.\n- Notify once when sharing enters a conflict-paused state. Retries remain silent.\n- Reset notification deduplication after recovery so a later conflict can notify again.\n- Notification failures and headless environments never block operations.\n- Status and doctor report the whole-setup pause, conflicting paths, resolution commands, and last successful application. Local-history and backup health remain distinct.\n\n### Existing review findings\n\nReverify every outstanding finding against current heads; fix valid issues in the earliest owning PR and propagate changes upward.\n\nPrioritize stale pull plans overwriting newer saved edits, missing synchronization baselines for initially identical files, declined-origin state leakage, portable config-directory mapping, and permission-metadata consistency. Validate automated findings rather than accepting them solely because a review tool reported them.\n\nKeep encrypted backups explicitly deferred and rejected when requested; do not silently upload plaintext instead.\n\n## Stack and documentation\n\nMaintain the existing PR order:\n\n1. #12849 — foundation\n2. #12835 — rollback\n3. #12838 — services\n4. #12843 — watcher\n5. #12865 — origin/sync\n6. #12882 — automatic sync/onboarding\n\nUse isolated working branches, preserve unrelated work, and update the existing PR branches. Restack with expected-head checks and force-with-lease only where rebasing requires it; stop if unexpected pushes appear.\n\nUpdate CLI help, generated docs, setup examples, PR descriptions, and the existing blog PR to reflect whole-setup pauses and default-on notifications. Remove claims that unrelated files continue syncing during conflicts. Keep unsupported encryption clearly distinguished from shipped functionality and always lowercase “mise.”\n\n## Verification and completion\n\nAdd or update tests for:\n\n- One conflicted file blocking all shared publication and incoming application while local history, fetching, and eligible backups continue.\n- Resolving multiple conflicts incrementally without partially applying changes.\n- Saved or unsaved edits made after planning never being overwritten by a stale pull.\n- Initially identical machines establishing a baseline and correctly handling subsequent edits.\n- Configuration and referenced sources being validated before application.\n- Mid-application failure, recovery, and concurrent edits.\n- Notification defaults, explicit opt-out, deduplication, and unavailable notifiers.\n- Permission-only changes, selective-save permission isolation, and excluded throttled files.\n- Existing two-machine sync, offline recovery, rollback propagation, platform variants, templates, and local/remote bootstrap workflows.\n\nRun focused tests during development, repository-required lint/render checks before commits, and CI on every updated PR head. Inspect substantive failure logs rather than relying on aggregate status.\n\nReply to review threads with the fix and verification evidence; resolve only findings actually addressed or demonstrated invalid. Finish with all six PRs ready for review, a concise validation report, and explicit remaining limitations. Do not merge.\n\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0774e-73de-7f93-9ac2-a0803ed77c35","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788708025.310217,"turn_id":"01a0774e-7311-7183-bbe0-5d429a7b050b"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"use a worktree\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07767-6118-7bd3-b717-4e6e85624eef","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788709658.904918,"turn_id":"01a07767-5e9f-7c30-a85f-2921c05466b6"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"ok is there feedback on the prs that needs to be addressed?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0776b-d93f-7d41-9f8e-504e2242078c","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788709951.807571,"turn_id":"01a0776b-d6fe-7063-9528-850ccb33e91d"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"ok reply to false positives and address feedback, keep checking for feedback, failing checks, and merge conflicts until the entire stack settles\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0776f-8da7-74d3-b917-ecf1c7382bd6","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788710194.599302,"turn_id":"01a0776f-8b86-7383-9180-4a703e38ce72"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"how does the stack and blog post compare now?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a077bb-abe7-74c3-89b8-92056406f170","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788715183.079516,"turn_id":"01a077bb-ab0c-7253-9092-b7dbbd644e8d"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\n# Response annotations:\nEach item contains text selected from an earlier Codex response and may include a user comment. Treat items as Annotation 1, Annotation 2, and so on in array order. Use every selection as context and address every comment. For every annotation you address, include its inline directive `:codex-annotation{index=\"N\"}`, where N is its one-based array position (for example, `:codex-annotation{index=\"1\"}`). Do not use unstructured annotation labels.\n\u003cresponse-annotations\u003e\n[{\"text\":\"The blog promises executable configuration requires trust approval. That isn’t fully enforced for synchronized history.describe_command settings. This needs an implementation fix, not just softer wording.\",\"source\":{\"messageId\":\"msg_0749c281f1ff31a6016a9da1059b0487d08d2ef7615898cbcd\",\"startOffset\":564,\"endOffset\":768}}]\n\u003c/response-annotations\u003e\n\n## My request:\nwhat is this?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a077be-f5a1-71a1-8df1-09dbb6642280","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788715398.561845,"turn_id":"01a077be-f4a5-7821-9ab6-b14af70720cd"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"is this the claude -p thing?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a077bf-cc83-76f1-8526-2281e4a48883","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788715453.571856,"turn_id":"01a077bf-cb59-7973-a88e-65cb000207e9"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"is it an escaping problem potentially?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a077c0-1702-7192-9c2d-7d647bd679bf","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788715472.642674,"turn_id":"01a077c0-1625-7b33-8ede-bac0f178de43"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"ok what should we do?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a077c0-7063-77a0-8fd6-07e5afc55497","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788715495.523049,"turn_id":"01a077c0-6f87-7ab0-b43b-ae4da2f7b2ed"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"ok add that to one of the prs in the stack\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a077c1-4815-7332-be85-9750128b9011","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788715550.741295,"turn_id":"01a077c1-472f-7723-ad8b-101b0407bd85"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"well is this necessary? if a user is adding a dotfile repo they will be able to get shell execution for sure\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a077c1-de12-7b73-b385-8365376637f1","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788715589.138385,"turn_id":"01a077c1-dd3d-7a73-ba44-2d9518554995"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"i don't even think it deserves disclosure\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a077c2-9018-7bc3-bfbc-10703128b387","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788715634.712651,"turn_id":"01a077c2-8f37-78d3-a848-062401fb8a21"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"ok fix the blog post, then let's talk about remote preview, what is it?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a077c3-084e-7b52-aa78-c9f97c42b651","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788715665.486939,"turn_id":"01a077c3-077d-7841-9dc8-8aa22ff57ec9"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"explain the other discrepencies and give a proposed solution\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a077c4-9f31-7412-92ee-9955fe6a0a9c","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788715769.649301,"turn_id":"01a077c4-9e67-7912-a253-e8ba2cbac16a"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"how is the stack looking now?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07812-c2de-7160-954e-7f53482267a9","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788720890.590896,"turn_id":"01a07812-c0c9-7891-ab33-63f7eadd24a0"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"an agent is working on the encryption pr\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07816-138c-7551-8d60-b8a8db2b3631","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788721107.852073,"turn_id":"01a07816-12ae-7601-bfbc-cb79ce8a673b"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"no\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07817-59e8-7960-a2d1-cd1b85cb0c54","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788721191.400247,"turn_id":"01a07817-58e5-7452-b9ae-1628c2fc7906"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"what about from a product perspective or tricky parts of this, do you have any questions for me?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07817-b91d-7e20-ad4b-56c8e9e80bcb","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788721215.773665,"turn_id":"01a07817-b848-7bc1-a012-f7761e8dd7a5"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"prompt me for these questions and fix the PRs, leave the encryption one alone \n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07819-ad1a-7f33-b25e-f3ded8a99f95","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788721343.770661,"turn_id":"01a07819-ac32-7782-a512-d3e0a35b975e"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"because this is getting quite complex, tracking should be marked experimental, modify these existing prs to mark it as experimental and gate on ensure_experimental\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0781f-2c0f-70d0-ab95-2df647465a1c","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788721703.951924,"turn_id":"01a0781f-2b35-7f13-bd06-952e347cb9f8"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"be careful with backwards compatibility, this stack will be merged together in the same release and it's been a few days since the last release. be careful no backwards compatibility cruft is in this stack that isn't necessary since no users have this functionality and it will all be shipped together\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07821-e758-7e53-ab6c-912476eecc7f","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788721882.968288,"turn_id":"01a07821-e65a-79d3-8b70-98cd2b81d2d4"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"yes\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07822-24ab-7833-8602-5037b868e853","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788721898.667108,"turn_id":"01a07822-23d7-7c00-a58f-bd5acb0fe8dd"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"start building bro\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07822-8548-7572-99cf-678441d19269","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788721923.400499,"turn_id":"01a07822-8479-7bf3-a8d6-b1867ce0cd21"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"ok go\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07822-a4b6-7c33-b40d-8c77c0cb3567","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788721931.446517,"turn_id":"01a07822-a3e5-7e32-8185-08e4b3a34f79"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"what are the blog changes?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07846-621c-76c2-b3bb-60e76aab355c","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788724273.692029,"turn_id":"01a07846-5f24-7332-8e00-f405474b90b6"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"what did the other agent change?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07849-be29-72d0-a6d1-80a0905ddc84","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788724493.865263,"turn_id":"01a07849-bce5-7283-9aba-92d2015f49e5"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"push all the changes including yours\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0784a-f938-78c3-ac69-be0d9797d083","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788724574.520426,"turn_id":"01a0784a-f83d-7222-8d22-de51d10941f7"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"is there feedback on the stack?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0784c-5f1e-7bd2-9b4f-a9a0009f9809","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788724666.142911,"turn_id":"01a0784c-5dbd-7f21-b728-2d01af15e259"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"keep addressing feebdack until it settles, feel free to stop if you need clarification\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0784e-24d2-7bb2-8560-d5eae3ac2437","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788724782.290289,"turn_id":"01a0784e-23cc-77b0-8fe9-f11e1d8bfc76"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"can you add the mise logo to the notifications?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0785f-465f-7310-a873-7ace0e970def","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788725904.991502,"turn_id":"01a0784e-23cc-77b0-8fe9-f11e1d8bfc76"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"keep addressing feebdack until it settles, feel free to stop if you need clarification\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0786f-dbaa-7d32-9396-b6987365648d","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788726991.786784,"turn_id":"01a0786f-d930-7653-bdfb-564e4c117620"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\u003csend_user_message_question_reply\u003e\n[{\"questionItemId\":\"[\\\"request_user_input_async\\\",\\\"call_pFiietOWwlygFSZGWAfdn2DZ\\\",0]\",\"question\":\"One rollback edge case needs a product call: Git snapshots don’t record empty directories. Should rolling back a parent directory leave unrecorded empty folders alone, or should we extend history to track empty directories too? I recommend leaving them alone; explicitly selected empty folders can still be removed and restored with undo.\",\"answer\":\"Leave unrecorded empty folders alone\"}]\n\u003c/send_user_message_question_reply\u003e","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07882-4b8a-7412-ac9e-67ec16c0a066","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788728200.074042,"turn_id":"01a0786f-d930-7653-bdfb-564e4c117620"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"the agenti had working on the encryption prs is done so you should include that now in these checks\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a078bd-ed73-7143-ad39-8b7d6042e80b","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788732108.147861,"turn_id":"01a078ac-bf7f-7050-adcc-4d223220149d"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"include the entire stack, there's 2 more prs i think\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a078d8-935a-7a60-af1c-b62e81bb6e36","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788733854.554576,"turn_id":"01a078d8-8fe1-7512-8383-08263a40e40e"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"do the restacking then continue\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a078d9-c1c6-7a73-9d0e-508a84a6c830","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788733931.974587,"turn_id":"01a078d9-c0cd-7843-901a-b76dfa554ca0"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"continue\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a078e9-0bd0-7352-9776-934742e12f5c","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788734933.96846,"turn_id":"01a078e9-0aa3-77c0-86b8-2b3b452b2375"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"address feedback on 12849\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a078f8-4102-7ab2-a811-245aad9f210e","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788735930.626481,"turn_id":"01a078f8-3fd2-7e42-8df9-65ccfb36d343"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\u003csend_user_message_question_reply\u003e\n[{\"questionItemId\":\"[\\\"request_user_input_async\\\",\\\"call_XNimpNCFCnfNHBz2ulXKuJnx\\\",0]\",\"question\":\"The remote-bootstrap feedback proposes an explicit `mise bootstrap remote --experimental` flag, forwarded to the target and saved there after successful tracking setup so the watcher keeps working. Should I use that approach?\",\"answer\":\"Yes, explicit remote flag and persist after successful setup\"}]\n\u003c/send_user_message_question_reply\u003e","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a078f9-774f-7710-82cf-01ff2f9650ec","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788736010.063456,"turn_id":"01a078f8-3fd2-7e42-8df9-65ccfb36d343"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"to be clear, I'm merging the entire stack at once so it doesn't matter if things are out of order\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a078fa-5b9f-7830-b967-3cd13ac2291e","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788736068.511298,"turn_id":"01a078fa-5a84-7440-9577-23aa455db11f"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"do it\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a078fb-4350-76d0-b569-25ba2b6de937","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788736127.824504,"turn_id":"01a078fb-40d9-7670-ba7c-bd0e572f6034"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"look through the feedback on all the prs for everything we haven't addressed\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07911-3d77-7830-81c6-0225d63e5d8c","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788737568.119725,"turn_id":"01a07911-3a90-7e81-9b67-55385e610266"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"fix all of it\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07915-957f-77b1-b738-11dfe0dad5ff","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788737852.799027,"turn_id":"01a07915-9360-79c3-87a8-fdfef3d33ee1"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"did you see my feedback on [https://github.com/jdx/mise/pull/12882](https://github.com/jdx/mise/pull/12882)\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07918-4c37-7b81-b905-0d0d21ce0671","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788738030.647654,"turn_id":"01a07918-4b50-7e42-84e6-5d190d1687c0"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"ok do it all\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07918-b6d1-7b81-9be6-3a91275500c8","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788738057.937383,"turn_id":"01a07918-b5e9-7403-918f-42ff062b923a"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\u003csend_user_message_question_reply\u003e\n[{\"questionItemId\":\"[\\\"request_user_input_async\\\",\\\"call_yhN3JvHP4UZyxmTijA5JQzc0\\\",0]\",\"question\":\"One filename-policy question: should experimental tracking support non-UTF-8 filenames end to end, or explicitly reject them without changing their bytes? The current stack rejects them; full support would need to cover capture, sync, encrypted backups, and rollback together.\",\"answer\":\"Keep explicit rejection for now\"}]\n\u003c/send_user_message_question_reply\u003e","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0793e-63d1-7021-994f-006449acaa18","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788740527.057741,"turn_id":"01a07918-b5e9-7403-918f-42ff062b923a"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"i changed my mind about any of this being experimental, remove that and continue\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07945-184d-7910-87e8-0ecc0d0432ff","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788740966.477955,"turn_id":"01a07918-b5e9-7403-918f-42ff062b923a"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"is there new feedback or unaddressed feedback?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07956-eeeb-77f1-baf9-49cc376f0354","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788742135.531008,"turn_id":"01a07956-ebb4-7a12-9455-bbcc530120c6"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"if it's already been resolved you should comment on it so we know it's done, fix the unaddressed stuff now\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07959-472c-74c0-82ed-e7c98a4b852c","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788742289.196108,"turn_id":"01a07959-462a-7891-b88e-39300119e54f"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"i don't think the icon is working on the notifications, at least when they pop up during the e2e tests, can you also think through the notifications a bit more and make them a bit clearer? I find them a bit confusing\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0797e-40a0-7ff2-b94b-a3c743051206","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788744712.352278,"turn_id":"01a07959-462a-7891-b88e-39300119e54f"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\u003csend_user_message_question_reply\u003e\n[{\"questionItemId\":\"[\\\"request_user_input_async\\\",\\\"call_QlIbGCZXd1t3ftJaZrs59Q55\\\",0]\",\"question\":\"A reliable mise icon on macOS needs a small mise notification helper app, with its own notification permission. Should I add that, or keep the built-in AppleScript fallback without a custom icon?\",\"answer\":\"Add the mise helper app\"}]\n\u003c/send_user_message_question_reply\u003e","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0797f-bc39-7692-9b73-1642cdd6f32b","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788744809.529163,"turn_id":"01a07959-462a-7891-b88e-39300119e54f"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Revise the unreleased dotfile PR stack around **explicit tracking, one ordinary Git history, and normal origin synchronization**. Replace the design with separate local checkpoint history, filtered publication history, and remote recovery backups.\n\n**1. Require explicit tracking**\n\n- Remove implicit tracking of the global mise config directory, `dotfiles.root`, and referenced dotfile sources.\n- Managing or referencing a file must not automatically enroll it.\n- Explicit directory enrollment includes descendants subject to exclusions.\n- Allow explicit tracking of managed files or sources without conflicting with their deployment declarations.\n\n**2. Use one committed history**\n\n- Automatically commit changes to explicitly tracked files into the repository.\n- Synchronization pushes that same history. Do not construct a second, filtered shared-state history.\n- Preserve manual and automatic sync modes and their cadence. Manual mode delays pushing; accumulated intermediate commits are included when eventually pushed.\n- Keep live files in place and repository storage separate, without adding `.git` to home or application config directories.\n- Preserve safe concurrent publication and conflict handling. Do not silently overwrite divergent history.\n\n**3. Remove per-file sharing controls**\n\n- Every tracked file is eligible for publication. Files that should never reach the origin must not be tracked.\n- Remove `share`, variant-level sharing overrides, and tracking options such as `--no-share` and `--private`.\n- Do not provide a parallel local-only tracking mode.\n- Without an origin, the repository remains local. Connecting an origin makes its committed history eligible for synchronization.\n\n**4. Remove the separate backup mechanism**\n\n- Remove machine-specific recovery-ref uploads under `refs/mise-history/...`.\n- Remove `backup` policies, backup-specific flags and onboarding, historical-backup uploads, backup encryption, and recovery flows dependent on those refs.\n- Do not replace these with an opt-in backup system.\n- Preserve fresh-machine setup from the ordinary repository.\n\n**5. Preserve history and safe recovery**\n\n- Keep labeled before/after boundaries around external commands and mise operations, history browsing, diffs, file restoration, undo, and interrupted-operation recovery.\n- Represent tracked-file history and operation boundaries using the ordinary commit history wherever possible.\n- Operation-scoped protective snapshots may remain local when needed for safe undo, especially for untracked files an operation modifies. They must not enroll those files, enter pushed history, or become a second ongoing tracking system.\n- History failures around external commands must warn without preventing the command from running or replacing its exit status.\n\n**6. Preserve shared-file encryption**\n\n- Retain encryption for tracked files intended to be encrypted in the repository.\n- Encrypt their contents before they enter any publishable commit—not merely when preparing an upload.\n- Verify every reachable pushed commit for plaintext leakage, not just the latest tree.\n- Removing backup encryption must not remove shared-file encryption.\n\n**7. Update the unreleased stack directly**\n\n- Remove obsolete settings, flags, schemas, and code paths outright. No compatibility shims, deprecation period, or migration machinery for the unreleased design.\n- Audit setup-repository publication and fresh-machine bootstrap for dependencies on implicit config/source enrollment. Require explicit enrollment instead.\n- Update CLI help, onboarding, status, documentation, and tests to describe only the new model.\n- Recreate disposable development/test stores as needed rather than supporting the old unreleased format. Do not automatically delete personal local or remote data.\n- Explain that untracking a file stops future tracking but does not erase its previously committed versions.\n\n**8. Verify the complete behavior**\n\n- Untracked global configs and referenced sources are not automatically captured or published.\n- Explicitly tracked files automatically commit, sync, merge, and restore correctly.\n- Manual sync later pushes the accumulated ordinary commits.\n- No filtered publication history or separate recovery-ref uploads remain.\n- Operation-scoped snapshots of untracked files never enter published history.\n- Capture, undo, interruption recovery, encrypted-file synchronization, and fresh-machine setup still work.\n\nApply this consistently across the existing stack. The intended model is **explicitly track files → automatically commit changes → synchronize those commits with the origin**. Treat this as a simplification of the history architecture, not merely a change to backup defaults.\n\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0799f-09f3-7901-abf1-9b815d7f508c","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788746861.043795,"turn_id":"01a0799f-08d9-7022-9269-9fa5e6fb73c7"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"i think trace = true isn't necessary, i would expect users to do something like \"\\~/templates/\\*\\*\" = {mode = \"track\"}\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a079a2-9c02-7481-9025-90750250d576","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788747095.042136,"turn_id":"01a079a2-97bb-7262-b25a-15e196efde37"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"does it need glob enrollment? or can we just support directories?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a079a3-9f70-7373-9569-b8aa4d6e9e95","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788747161.456797,"turn_id":"01a079a3-9d2c-7c33-a60e-8128542e5a37"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"ok what was the other question you had about\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a079a3-dd03-7460-8e61-b030ff343a9c","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788747177.219104,"turn_id":"01a079a3-dc10-7202-976e-777891777e4d"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"we should retain it indefinetely, i question if we need to track any other state at all\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a079a4-3fdb-7263-92a5-635a063a2c34","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788747202.523818,"turn_id":"01a079a4-3edc-7182-8ed3-9e5767e1ffd7"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"ok make the plan\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a079a4-eed6-7f31-802f-1dee95fd882a","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788747247.318133,"turn_id":"01a079a4-eda5-7d03-a424-612ae1dcaff4"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"PLEASE IMPLEMENT THIS PLAN:\n# Simplify dotfile tracking to one Git history\n\n## Summary\n\nRevise the existing unreleased stack around:\n\n**Explicitly track files → automatically commit changes → synchronize those commits with origin.**\n\nGit is the sole durable file history, retained indefinitely. Remove filtered publication history, local-only tracking, machine backup refs, and backup encryption. Preserve shared-file encryption, native editing, platform variants, templates, bootstrap onboarding, and safe conflict recovery.\n\n## Tracking and repository model\n\n- Keep `[dotfiles]` entries with `mode = \"track\"`. Accept exact files and directories; directories include new descendants subject to exclusions. Do not add enrollment globs or `track = true`.\n- Remove implicit enrollment of global mise configuration, `dotfiles.root`, deployment outputs, referenced sources, and symlink targets. Tracking a symlink records the link; its target requires explicit enrollment.\n- Separate tracking observation from deployment ownership internally. A tracking directory may contain managed files or sources without deployment conflicts. Preserve genuine conflicts between deployment declarations.\n- Remove `share`, variant sharing overrides, `backup`, local-only tracking options, and their settings, flags, schema fields, and status output.\n- Exclusions prevent capture, not merely publication. Protected credential-file defaults must exclude files entirely rather than silently retain private history.\n- Store one bare repository outside live configuration directories. Never create `.git` in home or application configuration directories.\n- Each ordinary commit contains the tracked-file tree plus minimal repository-owned metadata for portable paths, enrollment, variants, encryption, and permissions. Do not commit wrapper snapshot trees, recovery journals, raw machine-local configuration, or separate publication representations.\n- Maintain a stable portable mapping independent of whether a file is also a deployment source or output. Reject enrollment that cannot be represented safely rather than silently making it local-only.\n- Untracking removes the file from future committed trees and enrollment metadata without deleting its live contents. Receiving that change likewise leaves live contents alone. Previously committed versions remain in Git.\n\nExample:\n\n```toml\n[dotfiles]\n\"~/.zshrc\" = { mode = \"track\" }\n\"~/templates\" = { mode = \"track\" }\n\n\"~/.gitconfig\" = {\n  mode = \"template\",\n  source = \"~/templates/gitconfig.tera\",\n}\n```\n\nOnly `.zshrc` and the template directory are tracked here.\n\n## Commits, synchronization, and encryption\n\n- Commit tracked changes directly to the ordinary local branch. Preserve autosave controls, debounce/backoff, explicit saves, and manual/automatic synchronization cadence.\n- Manual synchronization delays network publication—not commit creation. A later push includes all accumulated commits unchanged.\n- Fetch into ordinary remote-tracking refs. Use Git ancestry, fast-forwards, and merge commits; do not squash intermediate history or construct filtered shared-state commits.\n- Preserve the complete repository tree when capturing one machine’s files, including inactive platform variants and manual-save files whose changes have not been explicitly saved.\n- Non-fast-forward publication must fetch and reconcile again. Never silently force-push, discard divergence, or rewrite existing commits. Connecting unrelated nonempty histories must fail with actionable guidance rather than automatically replace either history.\n- Any unresolved conflict pauses publication and incoming application for the entire setup. Local commits and fetching continue. Record per-file resolution choices without applying a partial setup; invalidate stale choices after relevant local or remote changes.\n- Preflight the complete incoming application, including configuration and required sources, before writing. Revalidate both committed and unsaved live contents before application. Preserve concurrent user edits.\n- Keep default-on, once-per-pause notifications and clear status/doctor diagnostics. Remove backup health reporting; distinguish local commit health from synchronization health.\n- Move shared-file encryption into capture, before content enters the repository’s object database or any publishable commit. Preserve encrypted-file restoration, synchronization, and recipient handling; never fall back to plaintext.\n- Audit every commit reachable from the proposed pushed branch for encrypted-path policy violations, including intermediate and merge-parent history. Block publication if an encrypted path has reachable plaintext versions. Do not automatically rewrite history; explain that encrypting the latest version does not erase earlier plaintext.\n- Remove all machine recovery-ref uploads, backup encryption, backup onboarding, historical upload options, and ref-dependent recovery commands. Retain only encryption used by ordinary tracked-file commits.\n\n## Operations, recovery, and bootstrap\n\n- Represent labeled before/after boundaries for external commands and mise operations with ordinary commits and minimal commit metadata. Allow empty boundary commits where needed to preserve labels and pairing.\n- Do not publish raw command arguments, environment contents, or untracked-file recovery data as operation metadata.\n- Derive history browsing, diffs, restoration, and undo of tracked files from Git commits. Restoring files creates a new commit rather than resetting shared history; preserve explicit path selection.\n- Remove automatic expiration or compaction of reachable Git history.\n- Retain only operational bookkeeping needed for concurrency, pending conflict choices, watcher scheduling, health reporting, and crash recovery—not another versioned history.\n- Keep private, temporary write-ahead recovery data for mise-controlled multi-file writes, including untracked files those writes would replace. It must remain outside publishable Git objects and refs.\n- Delete temporary recovery data after successful completion or safe recovery. Never expire an unresolved interrupted transaction. If recovery encounters concurrent edits, preserve them and report the remaining action.\n- Do not retain completed-operation snapshots or provide historical undo for untracked files. External-command capture records explicitly tracked files only; history failures warn without preventing execution or replacing the command’s exit status.\n- Fresh-machine setup reads enrollment and path mapping from the ordinary repository. Explicitly enrolled files can be restored without requiring an implicitly captured global configuration.\n- Recreating tools, services, and template deployments requires users to explicitly track the relevant bootstrap configuration and sources. Onboarding must list missing requirements and offer explicit enrollment; it must not silently add them.\n- Preserve existing non-tracking `--from-git` workflows and remote bootstrap authentication/proxy behavior. Synchronizing commits must not implicitly execute bootstrap configuration.\n\n## Stack updates and verification\n\nModify the existing PR stack directly, without merging it. Remove obsolete unreleased formats and interfaces outright; introduce no compatibility shims, deprecations, or migration machinery. Rewrite backup-focused PR contents around the remaining shared-file encryption work as appropriate.\n\nUse isolated worktrees, preserve unrelated changes, restack with expected-head checks, and push with explicit leases where necessary. Recreate only identified disposable test stores; never automatically delete personal local stores or remote refs. Update help, generated schemas/docs, onboarding, examples, PR descriptions, and the existing blog PR to describe only this model.\n\nAcceptance tests must cover:\n\n- No implicit capture of configuration, deployment sources/outputs, or symlink targets; recursive explicit directory tracking and exclusions work.\n- Tracking and deployment overlap safely, including template sources and managed outputs.\n- Autosave produces ordinary commits; delayed manual sync publishes the same accumulated commit ancestry.\n- Two-machine fast-forward, divergent merge, concurrent push, whole-setup conflict pause, incremental resolution, and stale-plan protection.\n- Platform variants survive captures from other machines; manual-save and throttled files are not inadvertently committed.\n- Untracking preserves live files and historical commits.\n- Before/after command boundaries, exit-status preservation, tracked restoration/undo, and interrupted-write recovery.\n- Temporary recovery copies of untracked files never enter reachable commits or uploaded objects.\n- Encryption precedes Git storage; missing keys fail safely; historical plaintext blocks publication even when the latest tree is encrypted.\n- Fresh-machine and remote bootstrap work with explicitly enrolled configuration and sources, and report missing prerequisites clearly.\n- No filtered publication history, machine backup uploads, backup-specific interfaces, or automatic committed-history retention remain.\n\nRun focused tests during implementation, repository-required lint/render checks before commits, and CI on updated PR heads. Inspect substantive failures and address review feedback with verification evidence. Report remaining limitations explicitly; do not merge.\n\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a079ae-a618-7903-8617-6919142593ab","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788747884.05683,"turn_id":"01a079ae-a385-7291-ae0b-5125a375ea18"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"why did you stop?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a079d4-ff99-7cc3-ad6f-17b1f5fa807e","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788750397.337825,"turn_id":"01a079d4-fd71-7ee3-83b0-7789da2cb519"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"push your changes and continue\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a079d5-3bd7-70f3-8875-a5af8a0df00e","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788750412.75989,"turn_id":"01a079d5-3ae3-7f93-84b9-c273bb03fa17"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"keep working, finish the plan, then after that start working on pr feedback, failing checks, and merge conflicts\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a079e2-e03f-7571-89fb-cde35a0bbfb9","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788751306.815934,"turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"call_id":"call_VRmtajZYSUWdCF61YNK3qep2","id":"ctc_02be90ffdd5dff4a016a9e42f81e1887d09a2ac1d33ce71402","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '135,194p' src/system/history/sync/origin.rs\\nsed -n '780,850p' src/system/history/tracked.rs\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise\",\"max_output_tokens\":1600}));\ntext(await tools.write_stdin({session_id:93910,chars:\"\",\"yield_time_ms\":1000,\"max_output_tokens\":700}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1788756722.786786,"turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_VRmtajZYSUWdCF61YNK3qep2","id":"ctco_01a07a35-b8b2-7ec1-9d5d-fedcdba3be03","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1788756736.178245,"turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 5.1 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"a1d9a3\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000003125,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1223,\"output\":\"            format!(\\\"tracked ({})\\\", rest.split('/').next().unwrap_or(\\\"home\\\"))\\n        } else {\\n            \\\"sources\\\".to_string()\\n        };\\n        *streams.entry(stream).or_default() += 1;\\n    }\\n    miseprintln!(\\\"Published from this machine:\\\");\\n    if streams.is_empty() {\\n        miseprintln!(\\\"  (nothing shareable yet)\\\");\\n    }\\n    for (stream, count) in \u0026streams {\\n        miseprintln!(\\\"  {stream}: {count} file(s)\\\");\\n    }\\n    if let Some(upstream) = \u0026upstream {\\n        let upstream_files = super::reconcile::upstream(repo, Some(upstream))?;\\n        let mut present = 0;\\n        let mut differing = vec![];\\n        let mut incoming = 0;\\n        let roots = Roots::current();\\n        for (branch_path, file) in \u0026shared.files {\\n            match upstream_files.files.get(branch_path) {\\n                Some((_, oid)) if *oid == file.oid =\u003e present += 1,\\n                Some(_) =\u003e differing.push(branch_path.clone()),\\n                None =\u003e {}\\n            }\\n        }\\n        for branch_path in upstream_files.files.keys() {\\n            if !shared.files.contains_key(branch_path)\\n                \u0026\u0026 roots.locate(branch_path).path().is_some()\\n                \u0026\u0026 run::eligible(\u0026roots, tracked, branch_path)\\n                \u0026\u0026 !privacy::is_private_branch_path(branch_path)\\n            {\\n                incoming += 1;\\n            }\\n        }\\n        miseprintln!(\\n            \\\"Against the repository: {present} identical, {} differing (decided with `mise bootstrap dotfiles pull --take-remote|--keep-local`), {incoming} incoming to apply.\\\",\\n            differing.len()\\n        );\\n        for path in differing.iter().take(10) {\\n            miseprintln!(\\\"  differs: {path}\\\");\\n        }\\n    }\\n    if !shared.unshared.is_empty() {\\n        miseprintln!(\\\"Not shared:\\\");\\n        for unshared in shared.unshared.iter().take(30) {\\n            miseprintln!(\\\"  {}: {}\\\", display_path(\u0026unshared.local), unshared.reason);\\n        }\\n        if shared.unshared.len() \u003e 30 {\\n            miseprintln!(\\\"  … {} more\\\", shared.unshared.len() - 30);\\n        }\\n    }\\n    if !shared.overrides.is_empty() {\\n        miseprintln!(\\\"Privacy overrides (private by default, shared by a per-file declaration):\\\");\\n        for path in \u0026shared.overrides {\\n            miseprintln!(\\\"  {}\\\", display_path(path));\\n        }\\n    }\\n    miseprintln!(\\n        \\\"All committed versions of explicitly tracked files are eligible for synchronization. Untracking does not erase earlier versions.\\\"\\n    let is_link =\\n        std::fs::symlink_metadata(\u0026expanded).is_ok_and(|meta| meta.file_type().is_symlink());\\n    if is_link \u0026\u0026 let (Some(parent), Some(name)) = (expanded.parent(), expanded.file_name()) {\\n        let parent = if parent.as_os_str().is_empty() {\\n            Path::new(\\\".\\\")\\n        } else {\\n            parent\\n        };\\n        return dunce::canonicalize(parent)\\n            .unwrap_or_else(|_| lexical(parent))\\n            .join(name);\\n    }\\n    dunce::canonicalize(\u0026expanded).unwrap_or_else(|_| lexical(\u0026expanded))\\n}\\n\\n/// The home directory or above: never walked, never watched.\\npub(crate) fn is_refused_root(path: \u0026Path, home: \u0026Path) -\u003e bool {\\n    path == home || home.starts_with(path) || path.parent().is_none()\\n}\\n\\n/// A path that may not exist, in the form the tracked set uses: the\\n/// deepest existing ancestor resolved, the rest appended as written.\\npub(crate) fn normalize_missing(path: \u0026Path) -\u003e PathBuf {\\n    let path = lexical(path);\\n    let mut rest: Vec\u003cstd::ffi::OsString\u003e = vec![];\\n    let mut current = path.as_path();\\n    loop {\\n        if let Ok(real) = dunce::canonicalize(current) {\\n            return rest.iter().rev().fold(real, |acc, name| acc.join(name));\\n        }\\n        let Some(name) = current.file_name() else {\\n            return path;\\n        };\\n        rest.push(name.to_os_string());\\n        let Some(parent) = current.parent() else {\\n            return path;\\n        };\\n        current = parent;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// Where a chain of symlinks ends: the last link's target, which need not\\n/// exist (a target between two versions, say), in the tracked set's form.\\npub(crate) fn link_target(link: \u0026Path) -\u003e Option\u003cPathBuf\u003e {\\n    let mut current = link.to_path_buf();\\n    let mut seen = BTreeSet::new();\\n    for _ in 0..MAX_LINK_DEPTH {\\n        if !seen.insert(current.clone()) {\\n            return None;\\n        }\\n        let dest = std::fs::read_link(\u0026current).ok()?;\\n        let joined = if dest.is_absolute() {\\n            dest\\n        } else {\\n            current.parent()?.join(dest)\\n        };\\n        current = lexical(\u0026joined);\\n        if !current.is_symlink() {\\n            return Some(normalize_missing(\u0026current));\\n        }\\n    }\\n    None\\n}\\n\\nfn lexical(path: \u0026Path) -\u003e PathBuf {\\n    let mut out = PathBuf::new();\\n    for component in path.components() {\\n        match component {\\n            Component::CurDir =\u003e {}\\n            Component::ParentDir =\u003e {\\n                out.pop();\\n\"}","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"5e4e8a\",\"wall_time_seconds\":5.001730125,\"session_id\":93910,\"original_token_count\":297,\"output\":\"mise WARN  GitHub OAuth refresh was rejected (incorrect_client_credentials): The client_id and/or client_secret passed are incorrect.. Reauthorization is required; run `mise token github --oauth --refresh`\\nmise WARN  GitHub OAuth refresh was rejected (incorrect_client_credentials): The client_id and/or client_secret passed are incorrect.. Reauthorization is required; run `mise token github --oauth --refresh`\\nmise WARN  GitHub OAuth refresh was rejected (incorrect_client_credentials): The client_id and/or client_secret passed are incorrect.. Reauthorization is required; run `mise token github --oauth --refresh`\\nmise WARN  GitHub OAuth refresh was rejected (incorrect_client_credentials): The client_id and/or client_secret passed are incorrect.. Reauthorization is required; run `mise token github --oauth --refresh`\\n[build] $ cargo build --all-features\\n   Compiling mise v2026.9.1 (/Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise)\\nmbx[warning]: incremental state was not reused: absolute path has no stable cache mapping: /opt/homebrew/opt/openssl@3/lib\\nmbx[warning]: prediction was not restored: absolute path has no stable cache mapping: /opt/homebrew/opt/openssl@3/lib\\n\"}","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_02be90ffdd5dff4a016a9e4301da2487d08b907d3361d36bd6","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"},{"call_id":"call_X3vv1zCQFWrC66KPyJvZ5RdE","id":"ctc_02be90ffdd5dff4a016a9e430542f087d08bc441000759eed2","input":"text(await tools.apply_patch(\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-takeover/TAKEOVER.md\\n@@\\n-Latest continuation: pushed integration commits 694961144 and 3adf709ec.\\n+Latest continuation: pushed integration commits 694961144 and 3adf709ec.\\n*** End Patch\"));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1788756736.732823,"turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_X3vv1zCQFWrC66KPyJvZ5RdE","id":"ctco_01a07a35-d972-7092-b73f-b51f91ec7506","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1788756744.562822,"turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749"},"output":[{"text":"Script failed\nWall time 0.0 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"Script error:\napply_patch verification failed: Failed to find expected lines in /Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-takeover/TAKEOVER.md:\nLatest continuation: pushed integration commits 694961144 and 3adf709ec.","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_02be90ffdd5dff4a016a9e430acdec87d0a1e77fda2612e15c","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"},{"call_id":"call_0ZC3FLABdkhMWGkgGJQw7RU2","id":"ctc_02be90ffdd5dff4a016a9e430dedb087d0a293b0a781f2f4f5","input":"text(await tools.apply_patch(\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-takeover/ONE_HISTORY_CURRENT.md\\n+# Current one-history continuation (2026-09-06)\\n+\\n+User explicitly says finish the plan, then feedback/checks/conflicts. Do not stop at a green intermediate slice. Do not merge. Original mise PR heads still untouched; implementation is in `/Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise`, branch `codex/dotfiles-one-history`.\\n+\\n+Latest integration push: `0bba94027` (push94883 verified). Previous `3adf709ec` includes manifest-only ordinary commit reading, graph primitives, decrypted restoration, removal of track --local, generated CLI docs. Blog PR99 pushed `72afed0` (push96894 verified); `/Users/jdx/src/blog-dotfiles-history` clean after one-history update. Hugo0.165.0 build passed. Blog still requires final factual review after implementation, including old example output counts.\\n+\\n+`0bba94027` removes filtered publication builder and refs/setup/publish. Runtime publish builds from ordinary HEAD with Graph::Heads/Candidate and audits candidate ancestry. Complete raw Git merge-tree must match already-applied local tree before adopting a merge; otherwise publication stops safely. Removed publication-time encryption delta/index code; encryption inventory now comes from manifest. Only format1 is supported. share comparison reads decoded transient objects with variant-aware tree paths. Capture dedup uses committed tree and modes, not machine-local coverage (coverage comparisons previously added a spurious empty commit on every sync).\\n+\\n+Verified: runtime publication unit tests2/2 PASS19798; encryption files tests5/5 PASS31999; manual ordinary-sync e2e initially failed39254 on spurious empty commits, fixed coverage comparison, PASS28538. Test verifies exact intermediate/local/remote commit identities, no extra commits on repeated sync, no separate refs, no implicit config capture, and encrypted commits identical before/after push with plaintext absent in both repositories. lint-fix11549 and render:usage45236 PASS. Dead-code warnings still remain; not Clippy clean.\\n+\\n+Current UNCOMMITTED continuation: `sync/run.rs` prepare derives baseline from common Git ancestry instead of persisted ack state; removes prepare's sync_state argument. `sync/reconcile.rs` early identical-saved/remote handling. New `e2e/cli/test_dotfiles_ordinary_two_machine` clones an ordinary bare store into a disposable second machine, connects, discards its operational sync-state cache, then fetches/pulls/publishes an incoming edit. Test session93910 running (build). Inspect result; do not assume success. No other running sessions known.\\n+\\n+Remaining architecture: complete same-DAG incoming adoption/merge including metadata and inactive streams; manifest-only fresh onboarding; effective enrollment reconciliation between Git and explicit configuration; CLI exact managed target overlap; minimal commit metadata replacing full Checkpoint and Git notes; portable permission metadata; variant-aware restore and plaintext diff without Git storage; temporary recovery lifecycle and retaining unresolved crash transactions; obsolete types/privacy paths/dead code; docs/blog/help audit; original PR distribution/restack with saved leases, CI and feedback. Existing graph merge currently blocks changes in repository-owned metadata because application only handles eligible live paths; encrypted divergent merges also need resolved ciphertext overlays after complete validation. Current baseline handles unique merge bases but criss-cross virtual-base reconciliation is still incomplete.\\n+\\n+Potential next internal design (not implemented): retain committed manifest enrollment as authority, apply deltas from explicitly changed local declarations using a private replaceable last-observed-declaration map. This avoids re-enrolling remotely untracked files from unchanged local config, and supports manifest-only machines without implicitly tracking global config. Must not create second file history or migration support. CLI exact managed-target tracking can use a dedicated global conf.d tracking declaration so deployment key is not overwritten; assess together with untrack and config precedence.\\n*** End Patch\"));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1788756745.476351,"turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_0ZC3FLABdkhMWGkgGJQw7RU2","id":"ctco_01a07a36-5a3c-7460-972e-e9f142c2a31e","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1788756777.532488,"turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{}","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_02be90ffdd5dff4a016a9e432befdc87d08a45f9f86ccff315","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749"},"summary":[{"text":"**Checking remaining test results**","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_02be90ffdd5dff4a016a9e4342121c87d0a94a7d0327710663","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749"},"summary":[{"text":"**Checking remaining test results**","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},{"call_id":"call_kY0Qt2XhHvLflHm73wLh73l9","id":"ctc_02be90ffdd5dff4a016a9e43435e7487d0b202e59a579c2492","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rg -n 'pub.*fn before|before\\\\(\u0026' src/system/history/scope.rs\\nsed -n '521,563p' src/system/history/sync/apply.rs\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise\",\"max_output_tokens\":1000}));\ntext(await tools.write_stdin({session_id:93910,chars:\"\",\"yield_time_ms\":1000,\"max_output_tokens\":1500}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1788756778.384208,"turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_kY0Qt2XhHvLflHm73wLh73l9","id":"ctco_01a07a36-c7ce-7401-bfb4-56ea461c12fe","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1788756805.582536,"turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"c6f7b8\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000005459,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":472,\"output\":\"225:    pub(crate) fn before(\u0026self) -\u003e Option\u003c(u64, String)\u003e {\\n233:    pub(crate) fn recapture_before(\u0026self) -\u003e Result\u003c()\u003e {\\n403:    fn capture_before(\u0026mut self, id: u64) {\\n    tracked: \u0026TrackedSet,\\n    sync_state: \u0026state::SyncState,\\n    step: \u0026Step,\\n    take_remote: bool,\\n) -\u003e Result\u003cOption\u003cString\u003e\u003e {\\n    let expected = step.pending.local.clone();\\n    if saved_object(repo, tracked, \u0026step.path)? != expected {\\n        return Ok(Some(\\n            \\\"local saved version changed since planning; run sync again\\\".into(),\\n        ));\\n    }\\n    if !take_remote \u0026\u0026 live_object(repo, \u0026step.path)? != expected {\\n        return Ok(Some(\\n            \\\"local file changed since planning; save or resolve it first\\\".into(),\\n        ));\\n    }\\n    // an incoming configuration file must at least parse\\n    if step.pending.configuration\\n        \u0026\u0026 step.path.extension().is_some_and(|ext| ext == \\\"toml\\\")\\n        \u0026\u0026 let Some((_, oid)) = \u0026step.pending.object\\n    {\\n        let bytes = repo.cat_object(oid)?;\\n        if let Err(err) = toml::from_str::\u003ctoml::Value\u003e(\u0026String::from_utf8_lossy(\u0026bytes)) {\\n            return Ok(Some(format!(\\\"invalid merge: {err}\\\")));\\n        }\\n    }\\n    if !step.exists {\\n        return Ok(None);\\n    }\\n    // a directory is never replaced by a file from the repository\\n    if step.path.is_dir() \u0026\u0026 !step.path.is_symlink() {\\n        return Ok(Some(\\n            \\\"needs decision: a directory stands where the repository has a file; move it away first\\\"\\n                .into(),\\n        ));\\n    }\\n    // inside a user checkout: staged changes always hold; an unstaged\\n    // difference holds unless it is mise's own previous application\\n    let applied = sync_state\\n        .get(\u0026step.pending.branch_path)\\n        .and_then(|record| record.applied.clone());\\n    // an untracked file is not the checkout's: the ordinary check applies\\n    if let Some(status) = git_status(\u0026step.path)?\\n\"}","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"34e66f\",\"wall_time_seconds\":9.58e-7,\"exit_code\":1,\"original_token_count\":1937,\"output\":\"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 1937)\\nTotal output lines: 156\\n\\nmbx[warning]: result was not stored: rustc search path kind is not cacheable yet: native\\nwarning: function `decrypt_bytes` is never used\\n   --\u003e src/agecrypt.rs:178:21\\n    |\\n178 | pub(crate) async fn decrypt_bytes(ciphertext: \u0026[u8]) -\u003e Result\u003cVec\u003cu8\u003e, DecryptError\u003e {\\n    |                     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^\\n    |\\n    = note: `#[warn(dead_code)]` (part of `#[warn(unused)]`) on by default\\n\\nwarning: function `default_identity_file` is never used\\n   --\u003e src/agecrypt.rs:221:15\\n    |\\n221 | pub(crate) fn default_identity_file() -\u003e PathBuf {\\n    |               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\\n\\nwarning: function `generate_identity_file` is never used\\n   --\u003e src/agecrypt.rs:232:15\\n    |\\n232 | pub(crate) fn generate_identity_file(path: \u0026Path) -\u003e Result\u003cString\u003e {\\n    |               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\\n\\nwarning: function `resolve_recipient_arg` is never used\\n   --\u003e src/agecrypt.rs:296:21\\n    |\\n296 | pub(crate) async fn resolve_recipient_arg(arg: \u0026str) -\u003e Result\u003cVec\u003cString\u003e\u003e {\\n    |                     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\\n\\nwarning: function `restorability` is never used\\n   --\u003e src/agecrypt.rs:564:21\\n    |\\n564 | pub(crate) async fn restorability(recipients: \u0026[String]) -\u003e Option\u003cbool\u003e {\\n    |                     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^\