{"timestamp":"2026-09-07T05:21:59.051Z","ordinal":18756,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_02be90ffdd5dff4a016a9e49f1e24087d09bc2ba548dc4cfc6","status":"completed","call_id":"call_YFWDis5n8gcboBOmO4yMpJfs","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.apply_patch(\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise/docs/history.md\\n@@\\n committed versions.\\n+\\n+This also applies inside `capture -- command`: if the command untracks a file,\\n+the outcome commit does not save its later contents. The before commit remains\\n+available, and interrupted-command recovery does not enroll the file again.\\n*** End Patch\"));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '136,178p' docs/history.md\\nsed -n '1,80p' src/system/history/sync/files.rs\",workdir:\"/Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise\",max_output_tokens:1600}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749","create_time":1788758507.925149}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-07T05:21:59.065Z","ordinal":18757,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a07177-9855-71a2-89cd-4a9a37cdbfcb","turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-fda0181b-03d1-4975-90d4-db5e1584db67","changes":{"/Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise/docs/history.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -40,2 +40,6 @@\n \n+This also applies inside `capture -- command`: if the command untracks a file,\n+the outcome commit does not save its later contents. The before commit remains\n+available, and interrupted-command recovery does not enroll the file again.\n+\n ## What a checkpoint records\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise/docs/history.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1788758519064,"completed_at_ms":1788758519065}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-07T05:21:59.151Z","ordinal":18758,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a07177-9855-71a2-89cd-4a9a37cdbfcb","turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749","session_id":"01a07177-9855-71a2-89cd-4a9a37cdbfcb","root_turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749","response_id":"resp_02be90ffdd5dff4a016a9e49ebc51487d0a454110494b2fde7","usage":{"input_tokens":116794,"cached_input_tokens":116480,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":284,"reasoning_output_tokens":111,"total_tokens":117078},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":48262786,"cached_input_tokens":47417856,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":166162,"reasoning_output_tokens":65954,"total_tokens":48428948},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":330285106,"cached_input_tokens":322890240,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":941176,"reasoning_output_tokens":246110,"total_tokens":331226282}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-07T05:21:59.377Z","ordinal":18759,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a07177-9855-71a2-89cd-4a9a37cdbfcb","turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-e76387fa-4ec0-4c98-b02b-0fcfbb782091","process_id":"52379","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '136,178p' docs/history.md\nsed -n '1,80p' src/system/history/sync/files.rs"],"cwd":"file:///Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '136,178p' docs/history.md","name":"history.md","path":"docs/history.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,80p' src/system/history/sync/files.rs","name":"files.rs","path":"src/system/history/sync/files.rs"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"Then the current state of the affected paths is saved in a protective\ncheckpoint (`rollback-before`); the plan is verified against the working tree\nagain (an editor may have written meanwhile) and every path about to change\nmust be captured in that checkpoint as it is now, or the rollback stops\nwithout touching anything. Files are written one at a time, each journaled\nand recorded as affected as soon as it is written, and each checked once\nmore right before it is replaced (a file that appeared meanwhile stops the\nrollback there). Only afterwards do `[history.reload]` commands run — once per matching\nglob, resolved from the system and global configuration before the operation\nbegan, so nothing a rollback writes can change which commands run:\n\n```toml\n[history.reload]\n\"~/.config/hypr/**\" = \"hyprctl reload\"\n```\n\nA rollback is a new forward change: the outcome is a new checkpoint, the\nversion you left is still recoverable, and nothing is rewritten. Restoring a\nmise configuration file never runs bootstrap; the outcome says when\ndeclarations may differ from the applied setup.\n\n`mise bootstrap dotfiles undo` restores the tracked paths an operation changed,\nusing its before commit and leaving unrelated work alone. Undo itself creates\na new commit. Untracked files have no historical undo: temporary recovery\ncopies exist only to complete or safely recover interrupted writes, and are\ndeleted afterwards. Unresolved recovery is never expired; concurrent edits are\npreserved and reported for action.\n\n## Capturing an external command\n\n```sh\nmise bootstrap dotfiles capture --label \"omarchy update\" -- omarchy-update\nmise bootstrap dotfiles history --label \"omarchy update\"\nmise bootstrap dotfiles history diff --operation --patch\nmise bootstrap dotfiles history diff 42 --operation --patch\n```\n\n`capture` saves tracked files before and after the command and records the link\nbetween those checkpoints, the label, and whether the command succeeded. It runs\nthe command directly with inherited input, output, and environment; raw command arguments and environment contents are not committed. Use\n`-- sh -c '...'` for shell syntax. Capture failures warn and the command still\nruns with its own exit status. No-op and failed runs retain their checkpoint\npairs. Files with `autosave = false` are explicitly saved by this command too.\n//! Encryption before Git capture and process-local decryption for live files.\nuse std::collections::BTreeSet;\n\nuse eyre::{Result, WrapErr, bail};\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\n\nuse super::{layout, reconcile::Object};\nuse crate::{agecrypt, system::history::shadow::HistoryRepo};\n\nconst MAGIC: &[u8] = b\"mise-encrypted-file-v1\\n\";\n\n/// Raw bytes serialized as a MessagePack `bin`, whatever the serializer's\n/// default for `Vec<u8>` is.\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub(crate) struct Bytes(pub Vec<u8>);\n\nimpl Serialize for Bytes {\n    fn serialize<S: serde::Serializer>(&self, serializer: S) -> Result<S::Ok, S::Error> {\n        serializer.serialize_bytes(&self.0)\n    }\n}\n\nimpl<'de> Deserialize<'de> for Bytes {\n    fn deserialize<D: serde::Deserializer<'de>>(deserializer: D) -> Result<Self, D::Error> {\n        struct Visitor;\n        impl<'de> serde::de::Visitor<'de> for Visitor {\n            type Value = Bytes;\n            fn expecting(&self, f: &mut std::fmt::Formatter) -> std::fmt::Result {\n                f.write_str(\"bytes\")\n            }\n            fn visit_bytes<E: serde::de::Error>(self, v: &[u8]) -> Result<Bytes, E> {\n                Ok(Bytes(v.to_vec()))\n            }\n            fn visit_byte_buf<E: serde::de::Error>(self, v: Vec<u8>) -> Result<Bytes, E> {\n                Ok(Bytes(v))\n            }\n        }\n        deserializer.deserialize_byte_buf(Visitor)\n    }\n}\n\n/// Audit the complete proposed ancestry, not just the latest tree. A newly\n/// encrypted path cannot make its previously committed plaintext safe to push.\npub(crate) fn audit_history(\n    repo: &HistoryRepo,\n    head: &str,\n    protected: &BTreeSet<String>,\n) -> Result<()> {\n    let commits = repo.rev_list(head, usize::MAX)?;\n    let mut protected = protected.clone();\n    // Policy changes cannot hide older plaintext, including on a merge\n    // parent or a platform that this machine never activates.\n    for commit in &commits {\n        if let Some(manifest) = crate::system::history::manifest::Manifest::read(repo, commit)? {\n            protected.extend(manifest.encrypted_paths());\n        }\n    }\n    if protected.is_empty() {\n        return Ok(());\n    }\n    let mut checked = BTreeSet::new();\n    for commit in commits {\n        for entry in repo.ls_tree(&commit)? {\n            if !protected.iter().any(|path| {\n                entry.path == *path\n                    || entry\n                        .path\n                        .strip_prefix(path)\n                        .is_some_and(|rest| rest.starts_with('/'))\n            }) || !checked.insert((entry.path.clone(), entry.mode.clone(), entry.oid.clone()))\n            {\n                continue;\n            }\n            let object = (entry.mode, entry.oid);\n            let valid =\n                envelope(repo, &object, agecrypt::MAX_ENCRYPTED_BYTES)?.is_some_and(|outer| {\n                    outer.path == entry.path\n                        && matches!(outer.mode.as_str(), \"100644\" | \"100755\" | \"120000\")\n                        && outer.ciphertext.0.starts_with(b\"age-encryption.org/v1\\n\")\n                });\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"Then the current state of the affected paths is saved in a protective\ncheckpoint (`rollback-before`); the plan is verified against the working tree\nagain (an editor may have written meanwhile) and every path about to change\nmust be captured in that checkpoint as it is now, or the rollback stops\nwithout touching anything. Files are written one at a time, each journaled\nand recorded as affected as soon as it is written, and each checked once\nmore right before it is replaced (a file that appeared meanwhile stops the\nrollback there). Only afterwards do `[history.reload]` commands run — once per matching\nglob, resolved from the system and global configuration before the operation\nbegan, so nothing a rollback writes can change which commands run:\n\n```toml\n[history.reload]\n\"~/.config/hypr/**\" = \"hyprctl reload\"\n```\n\nA rollback is a new forward change: the outcome is a new checkpoint, the\nversion you left is still recoverable, and nothing is rewritten. Restoring a\nmise configuration file never runs bootstrap; the outcome says when\ndeclarations may differ from the applied setup.\n\n`mise bootstrap dotfiles undo` restores the tracked paths an operation changed,\nusing its before commit and leaving unrelated work alone. Undo itself creates\na new commit. Untracked files have no historical undo: temporary recovery\ncopies exist only to complete or safely recover interrupted writes, and are\ndeleted afterwards. Unresolved recovery is never expired; concurrent edits are\npreserved and reported for action.\n\n## Capturing an external command\n\n```sh\nmise bootstrap dotfiles capture --label \"omarchy update\" -- omarchy-update\nmise bootstrap dotfiles history --label \"omarchy update\"\nmise bootstrap dotfiles history diff --operation --patch\nmise bootstrap dotfiles history diff 42 --operation --patch\n```\n\n`capture` saves tracked files before and after the command and records the link\nbetween those checkpoints, the label, and whether the command succeeded. It runs\nthe command directly with inherited input, output, and environment; raw command arguments and environment contents are not committed. Use\n`-- sh -c '...'` for shell syntax. Capture failures warn and the command still\nruns with its own exit status. No-op and failed runs retain their checkpoint\npairs. Files with `autosave = false` are explicitly saved by this command too.\n//! Encryption before Git capture and process-local decryption for live files.\nuse std::collections::BTreeSet;\n\nuse eyre::{Result, WrapErr, bail};\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\n\nuse super::{layout, reconcile::Object};\nuse crate::{agecrypt, system::history::shadow::HistoryRepo};\n\nconst MAGIC: &[u8] = b\"mise-encrypted-file-v1\\n\";\n\n/// Raw bytes serialized as a MessagePack `bin`, whatever the serializer's\n/// default for `Vec<u8>` is.\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub(crate) struct Bytes(pub Vec<u8>);\n\nimpl Serialize for Bytes {\n    fn serialize<S: serde::Serializer>(&self, serializer: S) -> Result<S::Ok, S::Error> {\n        serializer.serialize_bytes(&self.0)\n    }\n}\n\nimpl<'de> Deserialize<'de> for Bytes {\n    fn deserialize<D: serde::Deserializer<'de>>(deserializer: D) -> Result<Self, D::Error> {\n        struct Visitor;\n        impl<'de> serde::de::Visitor<'de> for Visitor {\n            type Value = Bytes;\n            fn expecting(&self, f: &mut std::fmt::Formatter) -> std::fmt::Result {\n                f.write_str(\"bytes\")\n            }\n            fn visit_bytes<E: serde::de::Error>(self, v: &[u8]) -> Result<Bytes, E> {\n                Ok(Bytes(v.to_vec()))\n            }\n            fn visit_byte_buf<E: serde::de::Error>(self, v: Vec<u8>) -> Result<Bytes, E> {\n                Ok(Bytes(v))\n            }\n        }\n        deserializer.deserialize_byte_buf(Visitor)\n    }\n}\n\n/// Audit the complete proposed ancestry, not just the latest tree. A newly\n/// encrypted path cannot make its previously committed plaintext safe to push.\npub(crate) fn audit_history(\n    repo: &HistoryRepo,\n    head: &str,\n    protected: &BTreeSet<String>,\n) -> Result<()> {\n    let commits = repo.rev_list(head, usize::MAX)?;\n    let mut protected = protected.clone();\n    // Policy changes cannot hide older plaintext, including on a merge\n    // parent or a platform that this machine never activates.\n    for commit in &commits {\n        if let Some(manifest) = crate::system::history::manifest::Manifest::read(repo, commit)? {\n            protected.extend(manifest.encrypted_paths());\n        }\n    }\n    if protected.is_empty() {\n        return Ok(());\n    }\n    let mut checked = BTreeSet::new();\n    for commit in commits {\n        for entry in repo.ls_tree(&commit)? {\n            if !protected.iter().any(|path| {\n                entry.path == *path\n                    || entry\n                        .path\n                        .strip_prefix(path)\n                        .is_some_and(|rest| rest.starts_with('/'))\n            }) || !checked.insert((entry.path.clone(), entry.mode.clone(), entry.oid.clone()))\n            {\n                continue;\n            }\n            let object = (entry.mode, entry.oid);\n            let valid =\n                envelope(repo, &object, agecrypt::MAX_ENCRYPTED_BYTES)?.is_some_and(|outer| {\n                    outer.path == entry.path\n                        && matches!(outer.mode.as_str(), \"100644\" | \"100755\" | \"120000\")\n                        && outer.ciphertext.0.starts_with(b\"age-encryption.org/v1\\n\")\n                });\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":3917},"formatted_output":"Then the current state of the affected paths is saved in a protective\ncheckpoint (`rollback-before`); the plan is verified against the working tree\nagain (an editor may have written meanwhile) and every path about to change\nmust be captured in that checkpoint as it is now, or the rollback stops\nwithout touching anything. Files are written one at a time, each journaled\nand recorded as affected as soon as it is written, and each checked once\nmore right before it is replaced (a file that appeared meanwhile stops the\nrollback there). Only afterwards do `[history.reload]` commands run — once per matching\nglob, resolved from the system and global configuration before the operation\nbegan, so nothing a rollback writes can change which commands run:\n\n```toml\n[history.reload]\n\"~/.config/hypr/**\" = \"hyprctl reload\"\n```\n\nA rollback is a new forward change: the outcome is a new checkpoint, the\nversion you left is still recoverable, and nothing is rewritten. Restoring a\nmise configuration file never runs bootstrap; the outcome says when\ndeclarations may differ from the applied setup.\n\n`mise bootstrap dotfiles undo` restores the tracked paths an operation changed,\nusing its before commit and leaving unrelated work alone. Undo itself creates\na new commit. Untracked files have no historical undo: temporary recovery\ncopies exist only to complete or safely recover interrupted writes, and are\ndeleted afterwards. Unresolved recovery is never expired; concurrent edits are\npreserved and reported for action.\n\n## Capturing an external command\n\n```sh\nmise bootstrap dotfiles capture --label \"omarchy update\" -- omarchy-update\nmise bootstrap dotfiles history --label \"omarchy update\"\nmise bootstrap dotfiles history diff --operation --patch\nmise bootstrap dotfiles history diff 42 --operation --patch\n```\n\n`capture` saves tracked files before and after the command and records the link\nbetween those checkpoints, the label, and whether the command succeeded. It runs\nthe command directly with inherited input, output, and environment; raw command arguments and environment contents are not committed. Use\n`-- sh -c '...'` for shell syntax. Capture failures warn and the command still\nruns with its own exit status. No-op and failed runs retain their checkpoint\npairs. Files with `autosave = false` are explicitly saved by this command too.\n//! Encryption before Git capture and process-local decryption for live files.\nuse std::collections::BTreeSet;\n\nuse eyre::{Result, WrapErr, bail};\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\n\nuse super::{layout, reconcile::Object};\nuse crate::{agecrypt, system::history::shadow::HistoryRepo};\n\nconst MAGIC: &[u8] = b\"mise-encrypted-file-v1\\n\";\n\n/// Raw bytes serialized as a MessagePack `bin`, whatever the serializer's\n/// default for `Vec<u8>` is.\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub(crate) struct Bytes(pub Vec<u8>);\n\nimpl Serialize for Bytes {\n    fn serialize<S: serde::Serializer>(&self, serializer: S) -> Result<S::Ok, S::Error> {\n        serializer.serialize_bytes(&self.0)\n    }\n}\n\nimpl<'de> Deserialize<'de> for Bytes {\n    fn deserialize<D: serde::Deserializer<'de>>(deserializer: D) -> Result<Self, D::Error> {\n        struct Visitor;\n        impl<'de> serde::de::Visitor<'de> for Visitor {\n            type Value = Bytes;\n            fn expecting(&self, f: &mut std::fmt::Formatter) -> std::fmt::Result {\n                f.write_str(\"bytes\")\n            }\n            fn visit_bytes<E: serde::de::Error>(self, v: &[u8]) -> Result<Bytes, E> {\n                Ok(Bytes(v.to_vec()))\n            }\n            fn visit_byte_buf<E: serde::de::Error>(self, v: Vec<u8>) -> Result<Bytes, E> {\n                Ok(Bytes(v))\n            }\n        }\n        deserializer.deserialize_byte_buf(Visitor)\n    }\n}\n\n/// Audit the complete proposed ancestry, not just the latest tree. A newly\n/// encrypted path cannot make its previously committed plaintext safe to push.\npub(crate) fn audit_history(\n    repo: &HistoryRepo,\n    head: &str,\n    protected: &BTreeSet<String>,\n) -> Result<()> {\n    let commits = repo.rev_list(head, usize::MAX)?;\n    let mut protected = protected.clone();\n    // Policy changes cannot hide older plaintext, including on a merge\n    // parent or a platform that this machine never activates.\n    for commit in &commits {\n        if let Some(manifest) = crate::system::history::manifest::Manifest::read(repo, commit)? {\n            protected.extend(manifest.encrypted_paths());\n        }\n    }\n    if protected.is_empty() {\n        return Ok(());\n    }\n    let mut checked = BTreeSet::new();\n    for commit in commits {\n        for entry in repo.ls_tree(&commit)? {\n            if !protected.iter().any(|path| {\n                entry.path == *path\n                    || entry\n                        .path\n                        .strip_prefix(path)\n                        .is_some_and(|rest| rest.starts_with('/'))\n            }) || !checked.insert((entry.path.clone(), entry.mode.clone(), entry.oid.clone()))\n            {\n                continue;\n            }\n            let object = (entry.mode, entry.oid);\n            let valid =\n                envelope(repo, &object, agecrypt::MAX_ENCRYPTED_BYTES)?.is_some_and(|outer| {\n                    outer.path == entry.path\n                        && matches!(outer.mode.as_str(), \"100644\" | \"100755\" | \"120000\")\n                        && outer.ciphertext.0.starts_with(b\"age-encryption.org/v1\\n\")\n                });\n"},"started_at_ms":1788758519376,"completed_at_ms":1788758519377}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-07T05:21:59.471Z","ordinal":18760,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a07a50-eeae-7bb1-968a-0b42c85245f6","call_id":"call_YFWDis5n8gcboBOmO4yMpJfs","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.4 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"8350b8\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000003917,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1363,\"output\":\"Then the current state of the affected paths is saved in a protective\\ncheckpoint (`rollback-before`); the plan is verified against the working tree\\nagain (an editor may have written meanwhile) and every path about to change\\nmust be captured in that checkpoint as it is now, or the rollback stops\\nwithout touching anything. Files are written one at a time, each journaled\\nand recorded as affected as soon as it is written, and each checked once\\nmore right before it is replaced (a file that appeared meanwhile stops the\\nrollback there). Only afterwards do `[history.reload]` commands run — once per matching\\nglob, resolved from the system and global configuration before the operation\\nbegan, so nothing a rollback writes can change which commands run:\\n\\n```toml\\n[history.reload]\\n\\\"~/.config/hypr/**\\\" = \\\"hyprctl reload\\\"\\n```\\n\\nA rollback is a new forward change: the outcome is a new checkpoint, the\\nversion you left is still recoverable, and nothing is rewritten. Restoring a\\nmise configuration file never runs bootstrap; the outcome says when\\ndeclarations may differ from the applied setup.\\n\\n`mise bootstrap dotfiles undo` restores the tracked paths an operation changed,\\nusing its before commit and leaving unrelated work alone. Undo itself creates\\na new commit. Untracked files have no historical undo: temporary recovery\\ncopies exist only to complete or safely recover interrupted writes, and are\\ndeleted afterwards. Unresolved recovery is never expired; concurrent edits are\\npreserved and reported for action.\\n\\n## Capturing an external command\\n\\n```sh\\nmise bootstrap dotfiles capture --label \\\"omarchy update\\\" -- omarchy-update\\nmise bootstrap dotfiles history --label \\\"omarchy update\\\"\\nmise bootstrap dotfiles history diff --operation --patch\\nmise bootstrap dotfiles history diff 42 --operation --patch\\n```\\n\\n`capture` saves tracked files before and after the command and records the link\\nbetween those checkpoints, the label, and whether the command succeeded. It runs\\nthe command directly with inherited input, output, and environment; raw command arguments and environment contents are not committed. Use\\n`-- sh -c '...'` for shell syntax. Capture failures warn and the command still\\nruns with its own exit status. No-op and failed runs retain their checkpoint\\npairs. Files with `autosave = false` are explicitly saved by this command too.\\n//! Encryption before Git capture and process-local decryption for live files.\\nuse std::collections::BTreeSet;\\n\\nuse eyre::{Result, WrapErr, bail};\\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\\n\\nuse super::{layout, reconcile::Object};\\nuse crate::{agecrypt, system::history::shadow::HistoryRepo};\\n\\nconst MAGIC: &[u8] = b\\\"mise-encrypted-file-v1\\\\n\\\";\\n\\n/// Raw bytes serialized as a MessagePack `bin`, whatever the serializer's\\n/// default for `Vec<u8>` is.\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]\\npub(crate) struct Bytes(pub Vec<u8>);\\n\\nimpl Serialize for Bytes {\\n    fn serialize<S: serde::Serializer>(&self, serializer: S) -> Result<S::Ok, S::Error> {\\n        serializer.serialize_bytes(&self.0)\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nimpl<'de> Deserialize<'de> for Bytes {\\n    fn deserialize<D: serde::Deserializer<'de>>(deserializer: D) -> Result<Self, D::Error> {\\n        struct Visitor;\\n        impl<'de> serde::de::Visitor<'de> for Visitor {\\n            type Value = Bytes;\\n            fn expecting(&self, f: &mut std::fmt::Formatter) -> std::fmt::Result {\\n                f.write_str(\\\"bytes\\\")\\n            }\\n            fn visit_bytes<E: serde::de::Error>(self, v: &[u8]) -> Result<Bytes, E> {\\n                Ok(Bytes(v.to_vec()))\\n            }\\n            fn visit_byte_buf<E: serde::de::Error>(self, v: Vec<u8>) -> Result<Bytes, E> {\\n                Ok(Bytes(v))\\n            }\\n        }\\n        deserializer.deserialize_byte_buf(Visitor)\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// Audit the complete proposed ancestry, not just the latest tree. A newly\\n/// encrypted path cannot make its previously committed plaintext safe to push.\\npub(crate) fn audit_history(\\n    repo: &HistoryRepo,\\n    head: &str,\\n    protected: &BTreeSet<String>,\\n) -> Result<()> {\\n    let commits = repo.rev_list(head, usize::MAX)?;\\n    let mut protected = protected.clone();\\n    // Policy changes cannot hide older plaintext, including on a merge\\n    // parent or a platform that this machine never activates.\\n    for commit in &commits {\\n        if let Some(manifest) = crate::system::history::manifest::Manifest::read(repo, commit)? {\\n            protected.extend(manifest.encrypted_paths());\\n        }\\n    }\\n    if protected.is_empty() {\\n        return Ok(());\\n    }\\n    let mut checked = BTreeSet::new();\\n    for commit in commits {\\n        for entry in repo.ls_tree(&commit)? {\\n            if !protected.iter().any(|path| {\\n                entry.path == *path\\n                    || entry\\n                        .path\\n                        .strip_prefix(path)\\n                        .is_some_and(|rest| rest.starts_with('/'))\\n            }) || !checked.insert((entry.path.clone(), entry.mode.clone(), entry.oid.clone()))\\n            {\\n                continue;\\n            }\\n            let object = (entry.mode, entry.oid);\\n            let valid =\\n                envelope(repo, &object, agecrypt::MAX_ENCRYPTED_BYTES)?.is_some_and(|outer| {\\n                    outer.path == entry.path\\n                        && matches!(outer.mode.as_str(), \\\"100644\\\" | \\\"100755\\\" | \\\"120000\\\")\\n                        && outer.ciphertext.0.starts_with(b\\\"age-encryption.org/v1\\\\n\\\")\\n                });\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749","create_time":1788758519.470946}}}
