{"timestamp":"2026-09-07T05:22:48.266Z","ordinal":18770,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_02be90ffdd5dff4a016a9e4a09bff887d0a28bc05b3c4b5ee0","status":"completed","call_id":"call_0ZpBzIRwGVbmll7OuvY0jYrr","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.apply_patch(\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise/src/system/history/shadow.rs\\n@@\\n-        let mut result = self.capture_tracked_files(walk, recipient_strings, interactive)?;\\n         let mut manifest = walk.manifest.clone();\\n@@\\n         manifest.recipients.sort();\\n         manifest.recipients.dedup();\\n+        let mut result = self.capture_tracked_files(walk, &manifest.recipients, interactive)?;\\n*** Update File: /Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise/src/cli/dotfiles/origin.rs\\n@@\\n-///\\n-/// `set <url>` connects one repository that holds the shared setup branch\\n-/// and this machine's recovery refs. Before anything leaves the machine it\\n-/// prints exactly what will happen: the sync mode, what is shared per\\n-/// stream, what is not and why, what is backed up (in plain form, or\\n-/// encrypted with `--encrypt-backups`), names that look like secrets,\\n-/// private content already committed upstream, and how an existing\\n-/// repository would be adopted. The declaration goes to `[history.origin]`\\n-/// in the global config; the mode to `settings.history.sync`.\\n+/// `set <url>` connects the ordinary tracked-file repository to an origin.\\n+/// All committed history becomes eligible for synchronization, including\\n+/// intermediate commits made before connecting. Preview the sync mode and\\n+/// tracked paths before confirming. Encrypted-file policy is checked across\\n+/// every reachable commit; unrelated histories are never replaced.\\n+/// The connection is written to machine-local `[history.origin]` configuration;\\n+/// the mode is `settings.history.sync`.\\n*** Update File: /Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise/src/system/history/sync/mod.rs\\n@@\\n-                \\\"sync: the watcher publishes saved changes and fetches periodically. Any conflict pauses publication and incoming application for the entire setup; local history, fetching, and eligible machine backups continue. Incoming changes are preflighted together and applied with a protective checkpoint and recovery journal. Applying never runs `mise bootstrap` or renders templates. Run `mise bootstrap` when the new declarations need to be applied.\\\"\\n+                \\\"sync: the watcher publishes saved commits and fetches periodically. Any conflict pauses publication and incoming application for the entire setup; local commits and fetching continue. Incoming changes are preflighted together and applied with a protective checkpoint and recovery journal. Applying never runs `mise bootstrap` or renders templates. Run `mise bootstrap` when the new declarations need to be applied.\\\"\\n@@\\n-                \\\"fetch-only: the watcher only downloads the repository and other machines' recovery refs. Nothing is ever published, and no live file changes unless you run `mise bootstrap dotfiles pull`.\\\"\\n+                \\\"fetch-only: the watcher only fetches the origin branch. Nothing is ever published, and no live file changes unless you run `mise bootstrap dotfiles pull`.\\\"\\n*** Update File: /Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise/src/system/history/describe_command.rs\\n@@\\n-    /// A unified diff of the changed files that are backed up (never a\\n-    /// private file, never one with `backup = false`), cut at the limit.\\n+    /// A unified diff of changed unencrypted tracked files, cut at the limit.\\n*** Update File: /Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise/src/system/history/sync/run.rs\\n@@\\n-                // application, not abort fetching and eligible backups.\\n+                // application, not abort fetching.\\n*** Update File: /Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise/e2e/cli/test_dotfiles_encrypted_capture\\n@@\\n assert_fail \\\"git --git-dir=$repo cat-file -e $second_plain\\\"\\n+\\n+# An ordinary clone carries recipients in its manifest, independently of config.\\n+cat >\\\"$MISE_CONFIG_DIR/config.toml\\\" <<'TOML'\\n+[dotfiles]\\n+\\\"~/.private-config\\\" = { mode = \\\"track\\\", encrypt = true }\\n+TOML\\n+echo manifest-recipient-value >~/.private-config\\n+manifest_plain=$(git hash-object ~/.private-config)\\n+assert_succeed \\\"mise bootstrap dotfiles save\\\"\\n+assert_contains \\\"git --git-dir=$repo show HEAD:home/.private-config | head -1\\\" 'mise-encrypted-file-v1'\\n+assert_fail \\\"git --git-dir=$repo cat-file -e $manifest_plain\\\"\\n*** End Patch\"));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749","create_time":1788758535.21531}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-07T05:22:48.285Z","ordinal":18771,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a07177-9855-71a2-89cd-4a9a37cdbfcb","turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-0abd64f5-8a50-4a6d-aec1-327b4fc65f9a","changes":{"/Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise/src/cli/dotfiles/origin.rs":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -7,11 +7,9 @@\n ///\n-///\n-/// `set <url>` connects one repository that holds the shared setup branch\n-/// and this machine's recovery refs. Before anything leaves the machine it\n-/// prints exactly what will happen: the sync mode, what is shared per\n-/// stream, what is not and why, what is backed up (in plain form, or\n-/// encrypted with `--encrypt-backups`), names that look like secrets,\n-/// private content already committed upstream, and how an existing\n-/// repository would be adopted. The declaration goes to `[history.origin]`\n-/// in the global config; the mode to `settings.history.sync`.\n+/// `set <url>` connects the ordinary tracked-file repository to an origin.\n+/// All committed history becomes eligible for synchronization, including\n+/// intermediate commits made before connecting. Preview the sync mode and\n+/// tracked paths before confirming. Encrypted-file policy is checked across\n+/// every reachable commit; unrelated histories are never replaced.\n+/// The connection is written to machine-local `[history.origin]` configuration;\n+/// the mode is `settings.history.sync`.\n #[derive(Debug, usage_rs::Args)]\n","move_path":null},"/Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise/src/system/history/sync/mod.rs":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -99,6 +99,6 @@\n             Self::Sync => {\n-                \"sync: the watcher publishes saved changes and fetches periodically. Any conflict pauses publication and incoming application for the entire setup; local history, fetching, and eligible machine backups continue. Incoming changes are preflighted together and applied with a protective checkpoint and recovery journal. Applying never runs `mise bootstrap` or renders templates. Run `mise bootstrap` when the new declarations need to be applied.\"\n+                \"sync: the watcher publishes saved commits and fetches periodically. Any conflict pauses publication and incoming application for the entire setup; local commits and fetching continue. Incoming changes are preflighted together and applied with a protective checkpoint and recovery journal. Applying never runs `mise bootstrap` or renders templates. Run `mise bootstrap` when the new declarations need to be applied.\"\n             }\n             Self::FetchOnly => {\n-                \"fetch-only: the watcher only downloads the repository and other machines' recovery refs. Nothing is ever published, and no live file changes unless you run `mise bootstrap dotfiles pull`.\"\n+                \"fetch-only: the watcher only fetches the origin branch. Nothing is ever published, and no live file changes unless you run `mise bootstrap dotfiles pull`.\"\n             }\n","move_path":null},"/Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise/src/system/history/shadow.rs":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -168,3 +168,2 @@\n     ) -> Result<CaptureResult> {\n-        let mut result = self.capture_tracked_files(walk, recipient_strings, interactive)?;\n         let mut manifest = walk.manifest.clone();\n@@ -180,2 +179,3 @@\n         manifest.recipients.dedup();\n+        let mut result = self.capture_tracked_files(walk, &manifest.recipients, interactive)?;\n         result.tree = manifest.preserve_other_files(self, &result.tree)?;\n","move_path":null},"/Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise/src/system/history/sync/run.rs":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -859,3 +859,3 @@\n                 // A changed type or unreadable live file must hold incoming\n-                // application, not abort fetching and eligible backups.\n+                // application, not abort fetching.\n                 unsaved.insert(branch_path.clone());\n","move_path":null},"/Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise/src/system/history/describe_command.rs":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -39,4 +39,3 @@\n     removed: Vec<&'a str>,\n-    /// A unified diff of the changed files that are backed up (never a\n-    /// private file, never one with `backup = false`), cut at the limit.\n+    /// A unified diff of changed unencrypted tracked files, cut at the limit.\n     diff: String,\n","move_path":null},"/Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise/e2e/cli/test_dotfiles_encrypted_capture":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -25,2 +25,13 @@\n assert_fail \"git --git-dir=$repo cat-file -e $second_plain\"\n+\n+# An ordinary clone carries recipients in its manifest, independently of config.\n+cat >\"$MISE_CONFIG_DIR/config.toml\" <<'TOML'\n+[dotfiles]\n+\"~/.private-config\" = { mode = \"track\", encrypt = true }\n+TOML\n+echo manifest-recipient-value >~/.private-config\n+manifest_plain=$(git hash-object ~/.private-config)\n+assert_succeed \"mise bootstrap dotfiles save\"\n+assert_contains \"git --git-dir=$repo show HEAD:home/.private-config | head -1\" 'mise-encrypted-file-v1'\n+assert_fail \"git --git-dir=$repo cat-file -e $manifest_plain\"\n assert_succeed \"mise bootstrap dotfiles rollback ~/.private-config --to 1 --dry-run\"\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise/src/system/history/shadow.rs\nM /Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise/src/cli/dotfiles/origin.rs\nM /Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise/src/system/history/sync/mod.rs\nM /Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise/src/system/history/describe_command.rs\nM /Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise/src/system/history/sync/run.rs\nM /Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise/e2e/cli/test_dotfiles_encrypted_capture\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1788758568280,"completed_at_ms":1788758568285}}
