{"timestamp":"2026-09-07T05:32:44.922Z","ordinal":18988,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_02be90ffdd5dff4a016a9e4c6826f087d08e04e25666ad3ae9","status":"completed","call_id":"call_u8v57dy1Fehs3ywwQ8qY7fHQ","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '147,169p' docs/bootstrap.md\\nrg -n 'post-dotfiles|pre-dotfiles' e2e --glob '*' | head -12\",workdir:\"/Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise\",max_output_tokens:1500}));\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise/src/system/history/recovery.rs\\n@@\\n     let mut failures = vec![];\\n+    let mut blocked: Vec<&Path> = vec![];\\n@@\\n         let JournalEntry::PathChanged { path, prior, .. } = entry else {\\n             continue;\\n         };\\n+        if blocked.iter().any(|blocked| path.starts_with(blocked) || blocked.starts_with(path)) {\\n+            continue;\\n+        }\\n@@\\n         if let Err(error) = recover_path(state_dir, path, prior, after) {\\n+            blocked.push(path);\\n@@\\n     fn corrupt_preimage_does_not_replace_current_file() -> Result<()> {\\n@@\\n         Ok(())\\n     }\\n+\\n+    #[test]\\n+    fn a_failed_later_write_blocks_earlier_recovery_of_the_same_path() -> Result<()> {\\n+        let temp = tempfile::tempdir()?;\\n+        let root = std::fs::canonicalize(temp.path())?;\\n+        let path = root.join(\\\"config\\\");\\n+        std::fs::write(&path, b\\\"original\\\")?;\\n+        let original = PathSnapshot::capture_with(&root, &path, Capture::Full);\\n+        std::fs::write(&path, b\\\"first result\\\")?;\\n+        let mut journal = change(&path, original);\\n+        let intermediate = PathSnapshot::capture_with(&root, &path, Capture::Full);\\n+        std::fs::write(&path, b\\\"second result\\\")?;\\n+        journal.push(JournalEntry::PathChanged {\\n+            part: \\\"test\\\".into(), item: \\\"second\\\".into(), path: path.clone(), prior: intermediate,\\n+        });\\n+        journal.push(JournalEntry::Committed { seq: 2, after: PathState::observe(&path) });\\n+        // The user returned to the first result, but changed its permissions.\\n+        // It must not be mistaken for an earlier step's result and reverted.\\n+        std::fs::write(&path, b\\\"user result\\\")?;\\n+        assert!(recover(&root, &journal).is_err());\\n+        assert_eq!(std::fs::read(&path)?, b\\\"user result\\\");\\n+        Ok(())\\n+    }\\n*** Update File: /Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise/src/system/history/journal.rs\\n@@\\n         let prior = PathSnapshot::capture_with(&dirs::STATE, &path, capture);\\n+        if let PathSnapshot::Unrecorded { reason, .. } = &prior {\\n+            eyre::bail!(\\\"cannot safely change {} without a recovery preimage: {reason}\\\", display_path(&path));\\n+        }\\n*** End Patch\"));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749","create_time":1788759134.990319}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-07T05:32:45.003Z","ordinal":18989,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a07177-9855-71a2-89cd-4a9a37cdbfcb","turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-97a708de-b471-4840-be92-2392a2dd5e4f","process_id":"30980","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '147,169p' docs/bootstrap.md\nrg -n 'post-dotfiles|pre-dotfiles' e2e --glob '*' | head -12"],"cwd":"file:///Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '147,169p' docs/bootstrap.md","name":"bootstrap.md","path":"docs/bootstrap.md"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'post-dotfiles|pre-dotfiles' e2e --glob '*'","query":"post-dotfiles|pre-dotfiles","path":"e2e"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"`mise bootstrap --only dotfiles,tools`. `--only` and `--skip` are mutually\nexclusive.\n\nUse `mise bootstrap --update` to refresh system package manager metadata\nbefore installing packages (apk: `--update-cache`, apt: `apt-get update`) and\nupdate declared repositories. Check the [repo update rules](/bootstrap/repos.html)\nfor clean-worktree and fast-forward requirements.\n\nHook phases can also run before and after the built-in steps:\n`pre-packages`, `post-packages`, `pre-repos`, `post-repos`, `pre-dotfiles`,\n`post-dotfiles`, `pre-defaults`, `post-defaults`, `pre-user`, `post-user`,\n`pre-tools`, and `post-tools`. Hook commands support [Tera templates](/templates.html)\nusing the declaring config's context, including values such as\n<code v-pre>{{ config_root }}</code>, <code v-pre>{{ xdg_config_home }}</code>,\nand <code v-pre>{{ vars.name }}</code>.\n\nThe declarative steps compare the requested state with the host and apply\nneeded changes. Hooks and the `bootstrap` task run on every selected apply, so\nmake them safe to repeat. Bootstrap is a sequence, not a transaction: if a later\nphase fails, earlier successful changes remain. Fix the reported failure and\nrun bootstrap again.\n\n## Previewing changes\ne2e/config/test_schema_bootstrap_hooks:30:pre-dotfiles = \"echo pre-dotfiles\"\ne2e/config/test_schema_bootstrap_hooks:31:post-dotfiles = \"echo post-dotfiles\"\ne2e/cli/test_dotfiles_watch_throttle:170:# The operation is an apply whose pre-dotfiles hook holds the operation lock\ne2e/cli/test_dotfiles_watch_throttle:174:[bootstrap.hooks.pre-dotfiles]\ne2e/cli/test_bootstrap:296:[bootstrap.hooks.pre-dotfiles]\ne2e/cli/test_bootstrap:299:[bootstrap.hooks.post-dotfiles]\ne2e/cli/test_bootstrap:328:[bootstrap.hooks.post-dotfiles]\ne2e/cli/test_bootstrap:351:[bootstrap.hooks.post-dotfiles]\ne2e/cli/test_bootstrap:356:post_dotfiles_message = \"stale-post-dotfiles\"\ne2e/cli/test_bootstrap:363:post_dotfiles_message = \"rendered-post-dotfiles\"\ne2e/cli/test_bootstrap:369:[bootstrap.hooks.post-dotfiles]\ne2e/cli/test_bootstrap:380:layered_post_dotfiles_message = \"{{ vars.post_dotfiles_message | default(value='missing-post-dotfiles') }}\"\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"`mise bootstrap --only dotfiles,tools`. `--only` and `--skip` are mutually\nexclusive.\n\nUse `mise bootstrap --update` to refresh system package manager metadata\nbefore installing packages (apk: `--update-cache`, apt: `apt-get update`) and\nupdate declared repositories. Check the [repo update rules](/bootstrap/repos.html)\nfor clean-worktree and fast-forward requirements.\n\nHook phases can also run before and after the built-in steps:\n`pre-packages`, `post-packages`, `pre-repos`, `post-repos`, `pre-dotfiles`,\n`post-dotfiles`, `pre-defaults`, `post-defaults`, `pre-user`, `post-user`,\n`pre-tools`, and `post-tools`. Hook commands support [Tera templates](/templates.html)\nusing the declaring config's context, including values such as\n<code v-pre>{{ config_root }}</code>, <code v-pre>{{ xdg_config_home }}</code>,\nand <code v-pre>{{ vars.name }}</code>.\n\nThe declarative steps compare the requested state with the host and apply\nneeded change