{"timestamp":"2026-09-07T05:34:58.415Z","ordinal":19021,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a07177-9855-71a2-89cd-4a9a37cdbfcb","turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_02be90ffdd5dff4a016a9e4cffa6dc87d0a920a25fbb1bd117","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The first recovery tests pass: they cover restoring private preimages without Git storage, preserving concurrent edits, rejecting corrupt recovery data, and recovering replaced directories.\n\nI’m now testing a real interrupted bootstrap. I’m also preserving the distinction between interruption recovery and an ordinary failed bootstrap—an ordinary failure must not silently undo earlier completed phases."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1788759295610,"completed_at_ms":1788759298415}}
