{"timestamp":"2026-09-07T05:43:47.936Z","ordinal":19147,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a07177-9855-71a2-89cd-4a9a37cdbfcb","turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_02be90ffdd5dff4a016a9e4f1151f487d0ae5052482c34c8f6","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The interrupted-bootstrap test passes: a concurrent edit is preserved, its recovery journal remains available, and recovery finishes once the file matches the recorded state. Untracked preimages never enter Git.\n\nI also found that corrupt recovery records could previously be hidden by renaming them. I’ve changed that to report an error and retain the data, so corruption cannot look like successful recovery."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1788759825278,"completed_at_ms":1788759827936}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-07T05:43:47.938Z","ordinal":19148,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_02be90ffdd5dff4a016a9e4f1151f487d0ae5052482c34c8f6","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The interrupted-bootstrap test passes: a concurrent edit is preserved, its recovery journal remains available, and recovery finishes once the file matches the recorded state. Untracked preimages never enter Git.\n\nI also found that corrupt recovery records could previously be hidden by renaming them. I’ve changed that to report an error and retain the data, so corruption cannot look like successful recovery."}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749","content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-07T05:44:03.408Z","ordinal":19149,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_02be90ffdd5dff4a016a9e4f13f82487d0b18334b176f55801","status":"completed","call_id":"call_bciArFlA6rrVnRVQBRFWRyA6","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.apply_patch(\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-takeover/ONE_HISTORY_CURRENT.md\\n@@\\n Current UNCOMMITTED recovery slice: new `src/system/history/recovery.rs`; derives equality for PathSnapshot and nested structs, deterministic directory walker; scope calls recovery on failed/stale operations before writing/closing their outcomes and discards only completed journal sidecars not retained by other pending records. Recovery keeps plaintext outside Git, checks before/after state, preserves concurrent edits/missing-completion cases, verifies blobs before restore, handles file/link/directory preimages conservatively. Unit test session16942 currently running. No other running sessions. Review this slice carefully before committing: add overlapping/repeated-path failure guard, pending retention coverage, and e2e interrupted writes/normal operations. Populated directories cannot be replaced based only on PathState entry-count identity; report actionable failure instead. Need lint/render as appropriate, tests, commit/push. No new subagents.\\n+\\n+Recovery update: old16942 PASS4, 97009 PASS5, 74636 PASS6. Added overlapping-path failure guard, malformed path/blob validation, private temp comparison (no copies of concurrent edits retained), successful sidecar disposal, and required usable preimages before mise-controlled writes. `Pending.recovery` enum now Pending / UnfinishedWrites / Finished: interrupted batches recover; normally returned commands retain completed phases and verify only writes missing completion. `scope.finish_incomplete` used when sync's own recovery failed. New e2e `test_dotfiles_private_write_recovery` covers normal large untracked preimage disposal, killed bootstrap, later concurrent edit/retained journal, subsequent safe recovery, no Git plaintext, and ordinary returned hook failure retaining completed phase. PASS87985 on full current recovery enum; capture regression PASS41298 on prior boolean revision. Current last change: pending JSON reader now errors without quarantining malformed data or hiding directory-read failures; added seventh recovery unit test ensuring corrupt pending preserves sidecars. lint-fix session75136 running. After it finishes run recovery units again, inspect diff, commit/push recovery slice. No Rust changes while compiling. Major fresh-manifest enrollment, full incoming metadata adoption, minimal Git metadata/notes removal, portable permissions, preflight, stack distribution/CI/reviews still outstanding.\\n*** End Patch\"));\ntext(await tools.write_stdin({session_id:75136,chars:\"\",yield_time_ms:1000,max_output_tokens:1300}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749","create_time":1788759804.085603}}}
