{"timestamp":"2026-09-07T05:53:54.369Z","ordinal":19277,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a07177-9855-71a2-89cd-4a9a37cdbfcb","turn_id":"01a079e2-ddee-7920-adc1-13c441666749","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-7247d18e-6256-4dea-a066-c71ec24e4b3d","process_id":"76034","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n 'pub.*fn .*encrypt|struct Encryption|recipients' src/system/history/config.rs | head -25\nsed -n '90,127p' src/system/history/checkpoint.rs\nsed -n '340,372p' src/system/history/checkpoint.rs\nsed -n '363,405p' src/cli/dotfiles/track.rs"],"cwd":"file:///Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'pub.*fn .*encrypt|struct Encryption|recipients' src/system/history/config.rs","query":"pub.*fn .*encrypt|struct Encryption|recipients","path":"config.rs"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '90,127p' src/system/history/checkpoint.rs","name":"checkpoint.rs","path":"src/system/history/checkpoint.rs"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '340,372p' src/system/history/checkpoint.rs","name":"checkpoint.rs","path":"src/system/history/checkpoint.rs"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '363,405p' src/cli/dotfiles/track.rs","name":"track.rs","path":"src/cli/dotfiles/track.rs"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"mise WARN  GitHub OAuth refresh was rejected (incorrect_client_credentials): The client_id and/or client_secret passed are incorrect.. Reauthorization is required; run `mise token github --oauth --refresh`\n31:/// Public recipients shared by every encrypted dotfile.\n35:    pub recipients: Vec<String>,\n38:pub(crate) fn file_recipients() -> Result<Vec<String>> {\n39:    let mut recipients = Vec::new();\n44:                    \"trust the configuration before using its encryption recipients: {}\",\n48:            recipients = encryption.recipients;\n51:    Ok(recipients)\n}\n\n/// An open history store.\n#[derive(Debug)]\npub(crate) struct Store {\n    state_dir: PathBuf,\n    repo: Option<HistoryRepo>,\n    unavailable: Option<String>,\n    machine: Machine,\n}\n\nimpl Store {\n    pub(crate) fn open_in(state_dir: &Path) -> Result<Self> {\n        store::ensure_store_dir_in(state_dir)?;\n        let machine = store::machine_in(state_dir)?;\n        let (repo, unavailable) = match HistoryRepo::open_or_init_in(state_dir) {\n            Ok(Some(repo)) => (Some(repo), None),\n            Ok(None) => (None, Some(shadow::unavailable_reason())),\n            Err(err) => (None, Some(format!(\"{err:#}\"))),\n        };\n        let store = Self {\n            state_dir: state_dir.to_path_buf(),\n            repo,\n            unavailable,\n            machine,\n        };\n        // the index is a cache of the repository: rebuild it when it is\n        // missing but checkpoints exist\n        if !store::index_exists_in(state_dir)\n            && let Some(repo) = &store.repo\n            && !repo.checkpoint_refs()?.is_empty()\n        {\n            info!(\"history: rebuilding the checkpoint index from the repository\");\n            store.rebuild_index()?;\n        }\n        Ok(store)\n    }\n\n                continue;\n            }\n            let Some(record) = coverage\n                .entries\n                .iter_mut()\n                .find(|record| record.path == entry.display())\n            else {\n                continue;\n            };\n            if manual.promote.contains(&index) {\n                record.state = \"live\".into();\n                record.promotion = None;\n            } else {\n                record.state = \"saved\".into();\n                record.promotion = None;\n            }\n        }\n        if !draft.has_metadata()\n            && let Some((previous_checkpoint, tree)) = &previous_tree\n            && snapshot.as_deref() == Some(tree.as_str())\n            && previous_checkpoint.tree.modes == modes\n        {\n            debug!(\n                \"history: nothing changed since checkpoint {