ed local config, and supports manifest-only machines without implicitly tracking global config. Must not create second file history or migration support. CLI exact managed-target tracking can use a dedicated global conf.d tracking declaration so deployment key is not overwritten; assess together with untrack and config precedence.\n21\t1\tsrc/cli/dotfiles/untrack.rs\n10\t3\tsrc/system/files.rs\n27\t1\tsrc/system/history/checkpoint.rs\n1\t0\tsrc/system/history/mod.rs\n21\t2\tsrc/system/history/tracked.rs\n6\t0\tsrc/system/history/watch/runtime.rs\nM  src/cli/dotfiles/untrack.rs\nM  src/system/files.rs\nM  src/system/history/checkpoint.rs\nM  src/system/history/mod.rs\nM  src/system/history/tracked.rs\nM  src/system/history/watch/runtime.rs\n?? e2e/cli/test_dotfiles_manifest_enrollment\n?? src/system/history/enrollment.rs\n"},"started_at_ms":1788761315606,"completed_at_ms":1788761315606}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-07T06:08:35.653Z","ordinal":19577,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a07a7b-9945-7b80-a09e-3f5822e06872","call_id":"call_GoQhJb1qLDXHDJfmQkalJAre","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"1262c1\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000003458,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":2316,\"output\":\"# Current one-history continuation (2026-09-07)\\n\\n## Latest continuation\\n\\nLatest verified integration push: `017170657` (push44441 complete). Recovery slice committed/pushed; final recovery unit tests7/7 PASS66230, lint-fix PASS75136; private-write-recovery e2e PASS87985 and capture PASS41298 (before final corrupt-pending reader tightening). Do not reimplement recovery module.\\n\\nCurrent UNCOMMITTED next slice: scope::try_operation_lock and sync::run::capture_now skip capture nonblocking while a write operation owns files; recover stale journals before capturing. Added capture unit test. prepare preflights every incoming application, not only config changes, and marks all incoming paths invalid when required sources fail. New e2e `test_dotfiles_ordinary_preflight` has an untracked bootstrap config with explicitly tracked template source, ensures incoming source deletion pauses whole batch. lint-fix PASS70238. Running e2es61452 (ordinary_preflight + ordinary_two_machine) and unit31307 (sync::run::capture_tests); check results before modifying Rust. Major remainder unchanged: manifest-only fresh setup and effective enrollment authority, complete Git tree/metadata adoption, minimal commit metadata/notes removal, portable permissions, obsolete interfaces/types/dead helpers/tests, original PR distribution/restack/CI/reviews. Continue, do not stop at green slice.\\n\\nVerified integration push now `3725407ea`, following `b76cc22b8` (both pushes completed). `b76cc22b8` includes Git-derived sync baselines, ordinary saved comparison view (no privacy module), expected-head publication checks and accepted-resolution overlays, full two-machine conflict tests, and safe exact managed target enrollment under conf.d. Explicit overlap e2e and two-machine e2e passed; declaration concurrency unit tests2/2 passed. `3725407ea` fixes preview portable config root/active explicit enrollment (unit1/1 pass), untracking inside external capture and interrupted capture without re-enrollment, nested untrack lock deadlock, manual-save external before boundaries, committed recipient fallback before encrypting, and removes stale backup CLI help. Both capture and encrypted capture e2es PASS7978; render:usage PASS29570; lint-fix PASS48683. Existing original PR heads still untouched.\\n\\nCurrent UNCOMMITTED recovery slice: new `src/system/history/recovery.rs`; derives equality for PathSnapshot and nested structs, deterministic directory walker; scope calls recovery on failed/stale operations before writing/closing their outcomes and discards only completed journal sidecars not retained by other pending records. Recovery keeps plaintext outside Git, checks before/after state, preserves concurrent edits/missing-completion cases, verifies blobs before restore, handles file/link/directory preimages conservatively. Unit test session16942 currently running. No other running sessions. Review this slice carefully before committing: add overlapping/repeated-path failure guard, pending retention coverage, and e2e interrupted writes/normal operations. Populated directories cannot be replaced based only on PathState entry-count identity; report actionable failure instead. Need lint/render as appropriate, tests, commit/push. No new subagents.\\n\\nRecovery update: old16942 PASS4, 97009 PASS5, 74636 PASS6. Added overlapping-path failure guard, malformed path/blob validation, private temp comparison (no copies of concurrent edits retained), successful sidecar disposal, and required usable preimages before mise-controlled writes. `Pending.recovery` enum now Pending / UnfinishedWrites / Finished: interrupted batches recover; normally returned commands retain completed phases and verify only writes missing completion. `scope.finish_incomplete` used when sync's own recovery failed. New e2e `test_dotfiles_private_write_recovery` covers normal large untracked preimage disposal, killed bootstrap, later concurrent edit/retained journal, subsequent safe recovery, no Git plaintext, and ordinary returned hook failure retaining completed phase. PASS87985 on full current recovery enum; capture regression PASS41298 on prior boolean revision. Current last change: pending JSON reader now errors without quarantining malformed data or hiding directory-read failures; added seventh recovery unit test ensuring corrupt pending preserves sidecars. lint-fix session75136 running. After it finishes run recovery units again, inspect diff, commit/push recovery slice. No Rust changes while compiling. Major fresh-manifest enrollment, full incoming metadata adoption, minimal Git metadata/notes removal, portable permissions, preflight, stack distribution/CI/reviews still outstanding.\\n\\nEverything below is older context; do not repeat completed work.\\n\\nUser explicitly says finish the plan, then feedback/checks/conflicts. Do not stop at a green intermediate slice. Do not merge. Original mise PR heads still untouched; implementation is in `/Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-one-history/mise`, branch `codex/dotfiles-one-history`.\\n\\nLatest integration push: `0bba94027` (push94883 verified). Previous `3adf709ec` includes manifest-only ordinary commit reading, graph primitives, decrypted restoration, removal of track --local, generated CLI docs. Blog PR99 pushed `72afed0` (push96894 verified); `/Users/jdx/src/blog-dotfiles-history` clean after one-history update. Hugo0.165.0 build passed. Blog still requires final factual review after implementation, including old example output counts.\\n\\n`0bba94027` removes